Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:53:18-07:00","id":855303,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was also struck by the new Firstborn Hunter of Names, Sky Hunter, Wolf-Who-Whispers, and the Incandescent and Opalescent Twins. The Twins make me think they're the actual children of Urfarah with Luna and Helios.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see a writeup of The Mountain, and its Host Children. The story sounds like it'd be an interesting read.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not gonna lie, I'd just like to see everything you couldn't fit in the wordcount on the time period. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 03-29-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:56:19-07:00","id":855306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed#post855280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Dark Eras is out to backers and, with it, the Neolithic era covering Mage and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Criticisms? Any interest in me writing up some unofficial sample Pangaeans? Sadly I didn't have wordcount to do more than provide the basic Pangaean rules in the chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fox. I would love a short write-up on Fox. Don't even need stats or such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:18:25-07:00","id":855317,"title":"","content":"This setting was just incredible. Crossover done right in a big way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:22:08-07:00","id":855366,"title":"","content":"I haven't really checked out the Mage section but I wouldn't know much about it to begin with. I really like the Werewolf section, however, especially the different sects. The hints about Pangaeans are really cool. It has what I really want in a Dark Era, a lot of clues and hooks that can be used any time, while still having a nicely fleshed out setting area to 'play' in. I like the 'Depth' for the Border Marches as well.<br /> <br /> It would, obviously, be very cool to see some Pangean beasties written up.<br /> <br /> It would be <i>spectacular </i>to see one of the Firstborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:23:07-07:00","id":855367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855294#post855294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely loved it. The one thing that hooked me more than anything else was the offhand mention of the minor Firstborn; have Eater of Names and Sky Hunter been mentioned before, or are they new creations of yours?<br /> <br /> I'm itching to build a Lodge around Eater of Names as a bunch of Ghost Wolves who hunt the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. Looks like I need to wait a little longer to find out more. But something tells me I can expect to see a boat load of hacks and homebrew soon based on what I'm hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:47:00-07:00","id":855441,"title":"","content":"AUSPICES WERE ALWAYS A THING.<br /> <br /> SILVER WAS ALWAYS PAIN.<br /> <br /> EVEN THE PURE ARE FORSAKEN, FOR THE CHILDREN OF WOLF AND MOON SHALL KNOW NO HOME FORVER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:24:02-07:00","id":855463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855441#post855441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AUSPICES WERE ALWAYS A THING.<br /> <br /> SILVER WAS ALWAYS PAIN.<br /> <br /> EVEN THE PURE ARE FORSAKEN, FOR THE CHILDREN OF WOLF AND MOON SHALL KNOW NO HOME FORVER.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you know, Same old, same old for the Uratha. Nothing amazing happens for them. Everything is ordinary.<br /> <br /> #zomgthissettingyouguysitssogood","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:38:55-07:00","id":855468,"title":"","content":"I'm getting the vibe that I might never use another setting ever again. Don't have the book yet, but this is the setting I was looking forward to the most. I'm already dreaming up ways to use Cult mechanics to simulate building a tribe.<br /> <br /> Seeing any kind of Pangaean would be spectacular. Are there any details on Snake in the chapter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:17:19-07:00","id":855477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855463#post855463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you know, Same old, same old for the Uratha. Nothing amazing happens for them. Everything is ordinary.<br /> <br /> #zomgthissettingyouguysitssogood</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no place like home, there's no place like home...<br /> <br /> And worse, it might have been deliberate. Damn you, Mourners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T21:23:45-07:00","id":855479,"title":"","content":"Of a point of interest, to me, is the implication that the wolves trying to create the Gauntlet couldn't just kill Wolf to do it, they had to employ an extra means for it. I'm inclined to believe it worked that way, at least, so that leaves me wondering just <i>what</i> exactly they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:33:06-07:00","id":855502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855479#post855479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of a point of interest, to me, is the implication that the wolves trying to create the Gauntlet couldn't just kill Wolf to do it, they had to employ an extra means for it. I'm inclined to believe it worked that way, at least, so that leaves me wondering just <i>what</i> exactly they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Given the interconnectedness of it all, I wonder if the Wise provided assistance in this crazy work. I doubt we'd ever get a word on that, but it's interesting to think about. What would they demand, to help lay low Urfarah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:39:21-07:00","id":855504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855502#post855502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Given the interconnectedness of it all, I wonder if the Wise provided assistance in this crazy work. I doubt we'd ever get a word on that, but it's interesting to think about. What would they demand, to help lay low Urfarah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, I'm just trying to figure out what the stage looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:56:09-07:00","id":855507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855502#post855502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Given the interconnectedness of it all, I wonder if the Wise provided assistance in this crazy work. I doubt we'd ever get a word on that, but it's interesting to think about. What would they demand, to help lay low Urfarah?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty stone?<br /> <br /> I wonder where it is now. Werewolves would like to know too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:20:12-07:00","id":855532,"title":"","content":"Considering we have a Massive Wound said to house the bones of Father Wolf it gives solid ideas to his Heart being somewhere in the world. And we have a dude hearing the voice of Father Wolf and possessing powers directly effecting the nature of Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Man, that's a Tier 3 or 4 storyline just waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:28:24-07:00","id":855538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855532#post855532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering we have a Massive Wound said to house the bones of Father Wolf it gives solid ideas to his Heart being somewhere in the world. And we have a dude hearing the voice of Father Wolf and possessing powers directly effecting the nature of Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Man, that's a Tier 3 or 4 storyline just waiting to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this dude?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:36:37-07:00","id":855541,"title":"","content":"Nighthorrors: Wolfsbane<br /> <br /> Dude is claiming to be the reincarnation of Father Wolf and the Pure worship him. He has the ability(well had in First Edition) to directly wipe away derangements and boost Harmony score. <br /> <br /> He espoused the usual Pure rhetoric and all that expected of him, but he kept hearing Father Wolf's voice telling him to follow the Forsaken ethos instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:45:02-07:00","id":855545,"title":"","content":"I'm just thinking, if the Omphalos Stones create powerful Demenses, and Urfarah's corpse was the sight of the first Wound... What implications might that carry about Wolf's soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-30-2016, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T00:55:46-07:00","id":855554,"title":"","content":"Well, his corpse is located there and the Wound comes from the extreme act that happened there. Essentially because you have the First Pack and their eldest kids jumping in to kill a being of cosmic power. Its connected to the Maeljin of Violence, of course.<br /> <br /> Where his heart is actually located is up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:01:50-07:00","id":855557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855554#post855554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, his corpse is located there and the Wound comes from the extreme act that happened there. Essentially because you have the First Pack and their eldest kids jumping in to kill a being of cosmic power. Its connected to the Maeljin of Violence, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's the story (which is true!) told by modern werewolves. Of course, as we've seen, modern werewolves got some wires crossed at some point. I was trying to suggest as a cool alternate interpretation that maybe Wolf's soul stone is what created the first wound, and to ask what might it mean that his heart did something different than what other Pangeans' hearts do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855554#post855554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where his heart is actually located is up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>In modern times? Probably several places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:05:19-07:00","id":855609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855468#post855468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting the vibe that I might never use another setting ever again. Don't have the book yet, but this is the setting I was looking forward to the most. I'm already dreaming up ways to use Cult mechanics to simulate building a tribe.<br /> <br /> Seeing any kind of Pangaean would be spectacular. Are there any details on Snake in the chapter?</div> </div> </div> </div> One of Serpent's manifestations is mentioned in the section about javelins.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:58:11-07:00","id":855620,"title":"","content":"I have some ideas for what I'd like to do with Pangaea and its legacy. One of which is tying in what will be a Forsaken-ized version of the Mokol\u00e9 as Pangaean descendants.<br /> <br /> Re: Father Wolf and the Wound, I might have to use him as the vehicle for the Abyss-as-the-Wyrm thing I had going in other ideas. Even without that, I can only imagine something terrible beyond reasoning rising from that Wound to threaten the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:09:54-07:00","id":855626,"title":"","content":"Just started to read the Era, but I very liked how term <i>People</i> ( by Vinca ) become <i>People</i> ( by Uratha ) - makes this time very important to later werewolves culture. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:00:57-07:00","id":855798,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't take that <i>too </i>seriously. Basically every culture in history has a name in their native language that more or less translates to &quot;The People&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:03:39-07:00","id":855803,"title":"","content":"I think the decision to recontextualise the relationship with silver is an interesting one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:10:21-07:00","id":855811,"title":"","content":"Details? (Not a backer. Very curious. Definitely going to snap this up the second it becomes available for everyone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:14:20-07:00","id":855816,"title":"","content":"Uratha pre-Sundering have exactly the same weakness to Silver as modern-day Forsaken do. Despite those modern Forsaken thinking that it was a punishment levied by Luna for the Sundering. The worse version of it the Pure suffer isn't because they're not Forsaken, it's because they've removed their Auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:28:29-07:00","id":855832,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda conflicted on it. I mean, it removes some of the relatability from the Uratha mythology. It's not the curse of a bereaved deity, it's just the deity being a bit weird. The increased issues for the Pure aren't the result of defying their duty, it's what happens if you rip a part of yourself out. It's lot more mechanistic.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's bad, it's just different.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it does leave the question of why no one has told the modern Uratha. I mean, there are Lunes around, yeah they're odd but you'd think one of them might have clarified the issue at some point. Though that does leave the obvious option that Luna chooses not to let them know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:29:41-07:00","id":855833,"title":"","content":"There are a number of details in the chapter, like that revelation about Silver, that I find really interesting because they re-contextualize or strongly contrast with standard assumptions of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:41:12-07:00","id":855843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855832#post855832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, it does leave the question of why no one has told the modern Uratha. I mean, there are Lunes around, yeah they're odd but you'd think one of them might have clarified the issue at some point. Though that does leave the obvious option that Luna chooses not to let them know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunes might not know themselves, most of them are not likely the same ones shining down on Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:55:37-07:00","id":855853,"title":"","content":"I did kind of call &quot;the Pure dogma is a load of bollocks&quot; a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:01:53-07:00","id":855861,"title":"","content":"There's actually some validity to it now. If Father Wolf did create Pangaea, it is possible his resurrection can re-create it. The Moon-hating part of it doesn't really fit, but may be a reaction to Luna's long silence during the period when the Uratha had no home. One parent was dead, the other merely watched them silently.<br /> <br /> It's similar to the way the attitude towards the Abyss developed. What was once a natural thing is, thousands of years later, something to vilify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:38:20-07:00","id":855893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855832#post855832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda conflicted on it. I mean, it removes some of the relatability from the Uratha mythology. It's not the curse of a bereaved deity, it's just the deity being a bit weird. The increased issues for the Pure aren't the result of defying their duty, it's what happens if you rip a part of yourself out. It's lot more mechanistic.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's bad, it's just different.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it does leave the question of why no one has told the modern Uratha. I mean, there are Lunes around, yeah they're odd but you'd think one of them might have clarified the issue at some point. Though that does leave the obvious option that Luna chooses not to let them know.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's just the deity being a bit weird&quot; somehow fails to grasp the fact that the Warden Moon is quite <i>insane</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:17:47-07:00","id":855930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855893#post855893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;It's just the deity being a bit weird&amp;quot; somehow fails to grasp the fact that the Warden Moon is quite <i>insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient divinities filtered through generations and eons aren't going to stay true to their original conceptions, and a god of madness and mutability should not be in the business of correcting the record. Also, these are gods and spirits walking among men, in an age where they <i> are</i> the mechanisms and physics of the world. Ripping out auspice is a refusal of duty, whatever era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:23:43-07:00","id":855936,"title":"","content":"Is that an agreement or a rebuttal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:25:21-07:00","id":855938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855936#post855936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that an agreement or a rebuttal?</div> </div> </div> </div>It reads like a bit of both tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:28:22-07:00","id":855941,"title":"","content":"Hence asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:30:35-07:00","id":855944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855936#post855936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that an agreement or a rebuttal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I read it as an agreement plus additional reasoning to support your side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:51:00-07:00","id":856028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855893#post855893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's just the deity being a bit weird&quot; somehow fails to grasp the fact that the Warden Moon is quite <i>insane</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I hoped it would convey my actual point a little better (which rereading it it didn't). That the change alters and distances the relationship between the Uratha and Luna, but the former don't realise that. There's no meaning behind the silver bane (well, there may be but we don't know it), it's the whim of an unknowable deity. At least a curse means the being cares enough to hurt you, now it seems luna didn't care as much as the Uratha like to think.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't dislike that. It's an interesting choice and it definitely fits with a lot of the hints that the Shadow is a lot more cosmic horror than the whole spirit world idea would initially indicate. It's pretty definitely bringing to the forefront that the Uratha are humanising quite radically inhuman entities.<br /> <br /> Giving it some more thought, the fact I feel a little sad at the change is probably dimmly similiar to how a modern Uratha would feel to find out something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=855843#post855843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunes might not know themselves, most of them are not likely the same ones shining down on Pangaea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point I hadn't considered. Kinda obvious to be honest. I think I might have been assuming that a natural part of the Uratha having a relation to Luna was the silver bane would be obviously different to Luna cursing them with it... which doesn't follow at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:29:19-07:00","id":856041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856028#post856028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but I hoped it would convey my actual point a little better (which rereading it it didn't). That the change alters and distances the relationship between the Uratha and Luna, but the former don't realise that. There's no meaning behind the silver bane (well, there may be but we don't know it), it's the whim of an unknowable deity. At least a curse means the being cares enough to hurt you, now it seems luna didn't care as much as the Uratha like to think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I got the opposite impression of the relationship between the Uratha and Luna from the chapter.<br /> <br /> Luna blessed them with Auspice, regardless of its complementary curse, from the start. She keeps a watchful and active eye over the Uratha and the Shadow, and she calls upon her children to hunt trespassers from the outside void that make it past her watch. Her Lunes descend readily to give Renown, and seem more cooperative and involved with werewolves than they have ever been since. When the book describes the Warden Moon, she sounds like the divine parent who is closest to the Uratha, and not Urfarah.<br /> <br /> It's one of those really cool inversions or shifts of perspective that are all over the chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-30-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:04:08-07:00","id":856115,"title":"","content":"Question- what exactly are Pangaeans and how do they differ from everything else? I saw things in the Mage thread indicating they can travel the Astral Realms, and I know the Omphalii of the Wise are the hearts of Pangaeans, but how do they differ from Spirits and Uratha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:10:50-07:00","id":856121,"title":"","content":"They're mostly like spirits, but they're solid instead of being made of ephemera. They're the native beings of the Border Marches, the world that sits between the material and Shadow, until Father Wolf's death destroys it and turns it into the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:16:21-07:00","id":856166,"title":"","content":"Notably, in the Shadow, very high-ranking spirits represent broad or fundamental concepts and are attended by courts of lesser spirits representing more specific expressions of those concepts. It seems as though this is not the case with Pangaeans? The majority of the Pangaeans mentioned in the chapter embody a species of animal, with the only exception I can remember off the top of my head being Mountain. But seemingly the only Pangaean with something resembling a court is Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:43:59-07:00","id":856186,"title":"","content":"The sidebar does mention beings possibly related to Pangaeans, including shapeshifters &quot;resembling Wolf's children but with the forms of different animals.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:59:34-07:00","id":856190,"title":"","content":"Also, was there anything on Bull-Shifters? I think I remember someone saying that they were in the chapter as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:59:55-07:00","id":856191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856186#post856186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidebar does mention beings possibly related to Pangaeans, including shapeshifters &amp;quot;resembling Wolf's children but with the forms of different animals.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The last sentence of that paragraph implies the category being spoken of includes, even if not exclusive to, the Shan'iatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:06:48-07:00","id":856194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856186#post856186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidebar does mention beings possibly related to Pangaeans, including shapeshifters &quot;resembling Wolf's children but with the forms of different animals.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, I forgot about that sidebar. In any case, my point is that in Pangaea, rather than a complex hierarchy of spirits representing related concepts with the broader expressions closer to the top, you've got one single Pangaean representing a very broad concept, which can split off shards of itself. If these other shapeshifters are to their respective Pangaeans as Uratha are to Wolf, (and presumably as the Beshielu are to Rat and the Aslu are to Spider), then the shards don't have a place in the spiritual hierarchies, and don't have Rank unless granted it honorarily by spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:09:06-07:00","id":856196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856190#post856190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, was there anything on Bull-Shifters? I think I remember someone saying that they were in the chapter as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the story seeds. The Gudthabak are potentially angry once they hear that the Wise have a part of Bull's heart. They believe if they get it back they will be able to keep their dwindling people from dying out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  I forgot about their special method of reproduction. 03-30-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:58:06-07:00","id":856217,"title":"","content":"Huh- interesting. So the Uratha actually are a &quot;Wolf Host&quot;? Go figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:04:58-07:00","id":856220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856217#post856217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh- interesting. So the Uratha actually are a &quot;Wolf Host&quot;? Go figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not explicitly stated or anything. But, you know, Wolf, Rat, and Spider are all Pangaeans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:09:42-07:00","id":856224,"title":"","content":"The Wolf Hosts were in Wolfsbane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:12:19-07:00","id":856225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856217#post856217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh- interesting. So the Uratha actually are a &quot;Wolf Host&quot;? Go figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's a little blurrier than that. Basically, they seem to &quot;work&quot; better than the Azlu and Beshilu, for instance. They can shift forms at will, and are equally at home on either side of the Gauntlet. The Hosts can't move quite so freely, and the werewolves' metaphysics just seem more advanced. It's more like they are all descended from Pangaeans, but the manner of their descent as well as the nature of their progenitors varies quite a bit. Also, it's implied that the Uratha are actually natives of Pangaea, which is an interesting thought. Their ancestral realm is gone, or at least collapsed into a membrane between worlds. What if you could reopen it?<br /> <br /> Also, information on the Pangaeans implies that if Father Wolf's heart-soul was found or reassembled and returned to his carcass (which legend says lies rotting in the First Wound), he could be reborn. But would most werewolves <i>want </i>that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:20:30-07:00","id":856227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856225#post856225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, information on the Pangaeans implies that if Father Wolf's heart-soul was found or reassembled and returned to his carcass (which legend says lies rotting in the First Wound), he could be reborn. But would most werewolves <i>want </i>that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably something most werewolves wouldn't even be able to consider, that would be a huge undertaking. It would probably be easier to walk on the moon. But there is already a Lodge of Predator Kings dedicated to scouring both worlds for relics of Mother Wolf in an attempt to put them together and bring her back. If they found out about the heart-soul I doubt anything could stop them from at least trying.<br /> <br /> Unlikely to be something a Forsaken would do, but the Pure have a much more idealized vision of Mother Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:25:55-07:00","id":856231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856225#post856225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's implied that the Uratha are actually natives of Pangaea, which is an interesting thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get that. Wolf is a native of Pangaea, and the Uratha are descended from Wolf, but they're all born in the Flesh, from human parents.<br /> <br /> The First Pack might be native to Pangaea, but they're implied to be pretty different from later generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:28:43-07:00","id":856235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856231#post856231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Pack might be native to Pangaea, but they're implied to be pretty different from later generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're caught up in instinct, 'Snarling, snapping, and slavering,' 'unable to break themselves from the all-consuming hunt,' 'swarming at [Wolf's] heels.'<br /> <br /> Now they sound like hosts, or host-possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:31:10-07:00","id":856237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856121#post856121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're mostly like spirits, but they're solid instead of being made of ephemera. They're the native beings of the Border Marches, the world that sits between the material and Shadow, until Father Wolf's death destroys it and turns it into the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like the Strix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:43:00-07:00","id":856244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856237#post856237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like the Strix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... Not so much. The strix aren't ephemera, but they're not really solid either. And like I've been saying, it seems Pangaeans are all godlike in their own right (potentially with a Host of offspring), rather than running the gamut from <i>Muthra</i> to <i>Ilusahim</i>. I've long been a big supporter of the Strix as the Owl Host interpretation, but this Era pretty much disproves it, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:50:16-07:00","id":856251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856244#post856244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... Not so much. The strix aren't ephemera, but they're not really solid either. And like I've been saying, it seems Pangaeans are all godlike in their own right (potentially with a Host of offspring), rather than running the gamut from <i>Muthra</i> to <i>Ilusahim</i>. I've long been a big supporter of the Strix as the Owl Host interpretation, but this Era pretty much disproves it, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could be of something else. Not Owls, but Darkness.<br /> <br /> I like the Belial's Brood theories, personally. The Adversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:52:51-07:00","id":856253,"title":"","content":"It does say that they are, however, true natives of the Pangaea. Their natural weapons even count as banes for all Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gods of Pangaea, p. 58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though similar to spirits, Pangaeans are \u2014 along with werewolves \u2014 the true natives of the Border Marches.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A later section also refers to werewolves as &quot;Native Predators&quot; of Pangaea. This also makes sense: as half-flesh, half-spirit creatures, a realm that blends both seems perfect for werewolves. Distinct from their progenitor god, different from the Hosts, werewolves seem better adapted for the duality. Perhaps their grounding in mortal flesh gives them that edge, or allowed them to adapt to a changing world. And these make for interesting theories and possibilities. What makes werewolves different? Why did they survive?<br /> <br /> For example, even if in many ways they are &quot;Wolf Hosts,&quot; werewolves behave differently than other Hosts. Why? Possibly because it wasn't simply Father Wolf's essence scattered among lesser vessels. The Plague King and Spinner Hag didn't beget a new race, they just spread themselves across a legion of lesser progeny. But however it happened, the Pangaean Wolf God created a new race, rather than shattering his own soul. Now, of course, some theories contradict this, suggesting that <i>Urfarah</i> grew weaker with each generation of werewolves. But that may have been a time-based thing, or a result of his many battles, proving even gods are not eternal. Contradictions and impossibilities make mythic histories fun, anyway.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that werewolves are, in a way, the only true surviving Pangaeans who maintain any purity of their original essence. They haven't transcended flesh and blood to become creatures of living myth, nor have they become wholly like spirits. They remain werewolves, one of the last living legacies of the Border Marches. If they still survive, perhaps one day Pangaea may return, as well.<br /> <br /> (I'll be exploring ideas like that in my own game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:58:58-07:00","id":856257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856253#post856253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes werewolves different? Why did they survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Beshilu and Azlu Hosts seem to spawn from a single source, Uratha and the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Gudthabak </span></span></span>have other patrons. The Moon and the Sun, respectively. I don't recall much of the other 'Wayward Cousins.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the idea that werewolves are, in a way, the only true surviving Pangaeans who maintain any purity of their original essence. They haven't transcended flesh and blood to become creatures of living myth, nor have they become wholly like spirits. They remain werewolves, one of the last living legacies of the Border Marches. If they still survive, perhaps one day Pangaea may return, as well.<br /> <br /> (I'll be exploring ideas like that in my own game.) </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a fun one. I really want to play up the Pangaean aspect in my own games, but in scope the plots and concepts never really get too far beyond 'Tier 2,' and this seems like a larger scope game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:04:29-07:00","id":856260,"title":"","content":"I think somewhere along the line here, my message got misinterpreted. My initial intent was not to point out a parallel between the Uratha and the Hosts, but rather to point out a difference I observed between Pangaeans and Spirits, to elaborate on Dave's explanation of them being &quot;like spirits, but made of physical matter and native to Pangaea&quot;. That said, this is an interesting line of discussion, so I'm happy to continue it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856253#post856253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does say that they are, however, true natives of the Pangaea. Their natural weapons even count as banes for all Pangaeans.<br /> <br /> A later section also refers to werewolves as &quot;Native Predators&quot; of Pangaea. This also makes sense: as half-flesh, half-spirit creatures, a realm that blends both seems perfect for werewolves. Distinct from their progenitor god, different from the Hosts, werewolves seem better adapted for the duality. Perhaps their grounding in mortal flesh gives them that edge, or allowed them to adapt to a changing world. And these make for interesting theories and possibilities. What makes werewolves different? Why did they survive?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just have a different idea of what the word &quot;native&quot; means. I'll buy that they are Pangaean in origin, and that it's their true home. I suppose any further distinction is just me being pedantic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856253#post856253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, even if in many ways they are &quot;Wolf Hosts,&quot; werewolves behave differently than other Hosts. Why? Possibly because it wasn't simply Father Wolf's essence scattered among lesser vessels. The Plague King and Spinner Hag didn't beget a new race, they just spread themselves across a legion of lesser progeny. But however it happened, the Pangaean Wolf God created a new race, rather than shattering his own soul. Now, of course, some theories contradict this, suggesting that <i>Urfarah</i> grew weaker with each generation of werewolves. But that may have been a time-based thing, or a result of his many battles, proving even gods are not eternal. Contradictions and impossibilities make mythic histories fun, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, what fun would it be if the answer was as simple as &quot;they're the Wolf Hosts&quot;? You've got to keep some kind of mystery to it, which is why to me, the similarities between the Uratha and the Hosts just make the differences all the more intriguing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856253#post856253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that werewolves are, in a way, the only true surviving Pangaeans who maintain any purity of their original essence. They haven't transcended flesh and blood to become creatures of living myth, nor have they become wholly like spirits. They remain werewolves, one of the last living legacies of the Border Marches. If they still survive, perhaps one day Pangaea may return, as well.<br /> <br /> (I'll be exploring ideas like that in my own game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I fully agree. I just don't see &quot;Pangaean&quot; as necessarily meaning &quot;native to Pangaea,&quot; just as Chinese doesn't necessarily mean native to China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:19:37-07:00","id":856268,"title":"","content":"Among other things, I think I am going to have a Pangaean that lies slumbering in stasis awaken at some point, and a shift to the general metaphysical landscape. Something like the Gauntlet acting weird (already the Rat and Spider are at war in the city), and perhaps the fearful tremors of <i>something </i>approaching. The Gauntlet beginning to expand could be part of that, especially in response to the emergence of an actual Pangaean.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to tie it into the Saurilu, my Forsakenized versions of the Mokol\u00e9 from Apocalypse, though probably not in that same game. But it's something I want to write up some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:33:33-07:00","id":856273,"title":"","content":"What rank Pangean is Father Wolf? We know what Luna is, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:35:03-07:00","id":856274,"title":"","content":"Considering the Pangeans are described as pillars of the world, I'm not sure rank is a easy thing for them past 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:39:30-07:00","id":856276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856273#post856273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rank Pangean is Father Wolf? We know what Luna is, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the existance of Pangaea itself seems to be directly linked to Wolf's existance, I would feel comfortable saying he's the highest Ranking Pangaean. I don't know that I'd put his Rank at 10, but I certainly wouldn't Rank any denizens of the realm he created higher than him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:41:45-07:00","id":856278,"title":"","content":"I had an idea that in the far future when Earth is gone, Luna flies through space as the Vampire Moon. Tunnels and caverns dug through the moon are homes for the last of the Uratha, crowded with relics of other worlds and long-dead civilizations. There's only one Firstborn left, bound and mostly helpless but revered for its sacrifice and gifts. They're infiltrators and raiders when they can be, as the moon passes near solar systems, they find loci and powerful but dormant spirits on other planets and bring the Essence back to fuel their home and god and parent. Sometimes they've come across alien races but Luna is their only home and hope.<br /> <br /> The best of the best are chosen to be taught a special rite by the Firstborn. It sends them back to a time when the Uratha were at their strongest. Once there, they harvest Essence directly related to Luna, tearing brands of renown from their ancient, ancient ancestors and calling the sacred hunt on Lunes. It takes a while for them to sort of find a niche to fit in, but once they've gained a few Primal Urge they are basically like other Uratha. They really respect the Forsaken, and view the Predator Kings as contemptible.<br /> <br /> While they seem savage and cruel, they're trying to get Luna enough energy to survive the end of the universe. The past is done with, and they don't believe anyone really needs it more than them. Luna has assured them it's necessary and worth it.<br /> <br /> But when it comes to my actual games it's usually much more down to earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:48:46-07:00","id":856281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856273#post856273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rank Pangean is Father Wolf? We know what Luna is, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's described as the greatest Pangaean, though by the end of his life he struggled against the Plague King, Spinner Hag, and mightiest spirits. In his prime, he was probably at least as high Rank as Luna, so around 7-8, possibly as high as 9 at his peak. Father Wolf didn't just hunt monsters, he hunted <i>concepts</i>, the literal embodiments of an ancient world's wrath. He himself was the Hunt manifest in lupine form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:05:41-07:00","id":856290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856274#post856274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the Pangeans are described as pillars of the world, I'm not sure rank is a easy thing for them past 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that I want to explore in my games, and a feeling I'm starting to get, is that Pangaea, the Border Marches, are a shrinking remnant of the &quot;true&quot; nature of the world. That is, all was Pangaea, once, where flesh and spirit inhabited the same lands, Essence flowed as freely as water, and mighty spirits arose in places where myth and meaning manifested as one. The separation between worlds is an unnatural thing, but it began even before Wolf's death. The realm between shrank, but few even realized it or what it meant. Pangaea is the world as it is meant to be, interconnected, not sectioned off and robbed of its vital rhythms. Raw, vital, and pulsing from the lowest microbe to the greatest mountain with living Essence.<br /> <br /> Then the question becomes: What caused the Border Marches to recede in the first place? When did it happen? Can it be reversed, and what consequences would that have on the mortal world? (Hint: they'd be apocalyptic in scope. But what if that's the way the world is <i>meant </i>to be? How much do you risk, how many do you condemn to death and cataclysmic upheaval in order to &quot;save&quot; the world?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:21:46-07:00","id":856294,"title":"","content":"That's actually sort of what Awakening is about.<br /> <br /> At least, a common theme in Gnosticism which has permeated a lot of the new World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:02:18-07:00","id":856317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856290#post856290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that I want to explore in my games, and a feeling I'm starting to get, is that Pangaea, the Border Marches, are a shrinking remnant of the &quot;true&quot; nature of the world. That is, all was Pangaea, once, where flesh and spirit inhabited the same lands, Essence flowed as freely as water, and mighty spirits arose in places where myth and meaning manifested as one. The separation between worlds is an unnatural thing, but it began even before Wolf's death. The realm between shrank, but few even realized it or what it meant. Pangaea is the world as it is meant to be, interconnected, not sectioned off and robbed of its vital rhythms. Raw, vital, and pulsing from the lowest microbe to the greatest mountain with living Essence.<br /> <br /> Then the question becomes: What caused the Border Marches to recede in the first place? When did it happen? Can it be reversed, and what consequences would that have on the mortal world? (Hint: they'd be apocalyptic in scope. But what if that's the way the world is <i>meant </i>to be? How much do you risk, how many do you condemn to death and cataclysmic upheaval in order to &quot;save&quot; the world?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, let's focus on one receding realm at a time.<br /> <br /> We still don't know why the Ocean of Fragments started to recede in the Underworld, and that's now part of the canon CofD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:32:35-07:00","id":856352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856225#post856225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it's a little blurrier than that. Basically, they seem to &quot;work&quot; better than the Azlu and Beshilu, for instance. They can shift forms at will, and are equally at home on either side of the Gauntlet. The Hosts can't move quite so freely, and the werewolves' metaphysics just seem more advanced. It's more like they are all descended from Pangaeans, but the manner of their descent as well as the nature of their progenitors varies quite a bit. Also, it's implied that the Uratha are actually natives of Pangaea, which is an interesting thought. Their ancestral realm is gone, or at least collapsed into a membrane between worlds. What if you could reopen it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because Uratha are children of Pangean <b>and</b> Spirit Queen? Azlu and Beshilu sounds like simple children of one Pangean parent and animals of his &quot;family&quot;. Uratha are &quot;children&quot; of <i>at least</i> Wolf, Moon and humans. It of course does not contradtict the theory of Uratha progenitor being Idigam also.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856225#post856225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, information on the Pangaeans implies that if Father Wolf's heart-soul was found or reassembled and returned to his carcass (which legend says lies rotting in the First Wound), he could be reborn. But would most werewolves <i>want </i>that?</div> </div> </div> </div>How then who? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Souless Wolf, looking for his lost Soul</a>, to remake it in to Malejin Tainted Mother Wolf! ( Yes, finally I have mine endgame for Bale Hounds game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:57:49-07:00","id":856361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856121#post856121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're mostly like spirits, but they're solid instead of being made of ephemera. They're the native beings of the Border Marches, the world that sits between the material and Shadow, until Father Wolf's death destroys it and turns it into the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also possibility that Pangaeans are connected to Supernal and are survivors from Fall of reality. That;s why they have Arcana and their hearts works as Demesne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856290#post856290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that I want to explore in my games, and a feeling I'm starting to get, is that Pangaea, the Border Marches, are a shrinking remnant of the &quot;true&quot; nature of the world. That is, all was Pangaea, once, where flesh and spirit inhabited the same lands, Essence flowed as freely as water, and mighty spirits arose in places where myth and meaning manifested as one. The separation between worlds is an unnatural thing, but it began even before Wolf's death. The realm between shrank, but few even realized it or what it meant. Pangaea is the world as it is meant to be, interconnected, not sectioned off and robbed of its vital rhythms. Raw, vital, and pulsing from the lowest microbe to the greatest mountain with living Essence.<br /> <br /> Then the question becomes: What caused the Border Marches to recede in the first place? When did it happen? Can it be reversed, and what consequences would that have on the mortal world? (Hint: they'd be apocalyptic in scope. But what if that's the way the world is <i>meant </i>to be? How much do you risk, how many do you condemn to death and cataclysmic upheaval in order to &quot;save&quot; the world?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Border Marches = Primal Wild? Supernal World? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T04:16:44-07:00","id":856381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856352#post856352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How then who? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">Souless Wolf, looking for his lost Soul</a>, to remake it in to Malejin Tainted Mother Wolf! ( Yes, finally I have mine endgame for Bale Hounds game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Sounds like it'll be fun.<br /> <br /> Let's see, if I was going to do something with a grisly reanimated undead Father Wolf, I'm not sure what I'd do. I've thought about having him be possessed by something of the Abyss and rising as a dead Wolf God whose slavering maw opens into oblivion. Perhaps the Abyss <i>is </i>the First Wound, and at its heart lies the festering carcass of the greatest Pangaean. The nice thing about mythic history, and especially the time-defying breaking of the Time Before, is that you can really play around with different ideas.<br /> <br /> If I'm exploring my visions of Apocalypse elements in the Chronicles, Father Wolf would definitely play a part. Perhaps as a body for <i>Umarah</i>, the Wyrm, a vessel by which it might devour all creation and render it into nothing. Maybe the werewolves could prevent that, perhaps by restoring <i>Urfarah </i>before it's too late. Or maybe that would only worsen things, as <i>Urfarah </i>turns his rage to the modern world, perhaps to his own descendants. Another option might be to restore the Border Marches, or even take it further, and swell that realm until it encompasses the world. Maybe that's the way the world once was, the way it's supposed to be. Or maybe even that is a lie or half-truth. There's really a lot of potential to explore many story options here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:29:58-07:00","id":856405,"title":"","content":"Right, so, for starters I'm working on statting up the Pangaeans Fox and Harvest, and some sample spirits. As noted before, these are all unofficial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856257#post856257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Beshilu and Azlu Hosts seem to spawn from a single source, Uratha and the <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Gudthabak </span></span></span>have other patrons. The Moon and the Sun,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bNote that the gudthabak do *not* have the patronage of Helios during the Sundered World period.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:10:54-07:00","id":856419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856405#post856405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so, for starters I'm working on statting up the Pangaeans Fox and Harvest, and some sample spirits. As noted before, these are all unofficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks 1000% for having more than an animal Pangaean. Really looking forward to these.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn2.denofgeek.us/sites/denofgeekus/files/styles/insert_main_wide_image/public/4/63//vandal-savage-dc-legends-of-tomorrow.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bNote that the gudthabak do *not* have the patronage of Helios during the Sundered World period. </div> </div> </div>Okay, I wasn't sure about that. I thought that they had perhaps gained Helios' patronage later, which is why their numbers stabilized, but it looked like the last of the Possible Resolutions went through, so maybe they had already had it. Thanks for clearing that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:16:14-07:00","id":856424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856405#post856405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so, for starters I'm working on statting up the Pangaeans Fox and Harvest, and some sample spirits. As noted before, these are all unofficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Niiice.<br /> <br /> ... Would it be possible to see some of the Firstborn? I am <i>really curious </i>about Sky Hunter in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:12:34-07:00","id":856450,"title":"","content":"I am so happy with this end result. Hearing more about non-animal Pangaeans would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, so glad that I didn't accidentally end the thread. Sometimes I'll comment on one and it will immediately wither and die, so really glad it sparked a discussion instead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:46:12-07:00","id":856467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856361#post856361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Border Marches = Primal Wild? Supernal World? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very definitely no. The Fallen World is way too complicated for one-to-ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:48:46-07:00","id":856468,"title":"","content":"Damn, really wanted to see Great Mountain. I have a crazy idea that he's the God Machine and when Pangaea broke he was on the Flesh side. So he has to abide by the rules of this reality. Now the earthen works he forced people to build are Infrastructure, and the Aether he harvests to fuel his machinations is the naturally occurring essence of the mortal world. The earth elementals are now angels modeled after the Quashmallim. Madness ensues.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm definitely down for seeing Fox, though. After watching Teen Wolf and reading about the Utu Sizen from Skinchangers I was really thinking about Nogitsune being hunted down by Father Wolf, but his brother(Inari) begged for his life. So Father Wolf shattered him and forced the shards to serve those they had hurt the most. So these people have a shard of the Void Fox inside of them, and if their Integrity dips too low it takes over and the real fun begins.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see how Fox works and what I can do to use the story with him instead. Damn Mages. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 03-31-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:22:18-07:00","id":856491,"title":"","content":"So.<br /> Pangaeans can use Arcana.<br /> Some of the Changing Breeds, who are also half-spirit-half-flesh things can use Beast Magic.<br /> Interesting. Isn't it?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know the book is bad, but that doesn't mean it never existed. It IS worth thinking about.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:29:28-07:00","id":856493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856121#post856121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Pangeans]'re mostly like spirits, but they're solid instead of being made of ephemera. They're the native beings of the Border Marches, the world that sits between the material and Shadow, until Father Wolf's death destroys it and turns it into the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856225#post856225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's implied that the Uratha are actually natives of Pangaea, which is an interesting thought. Their ancestral realm is gone, or at least collapsed into a membrane between worlds. What if you could reopen it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall from the Summoners book something about <i>things</i> still living in the Gauntlet itself. How do these things tie together?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:40:47-07:00","id":856499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856491#post856491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.<br /> Pangaeans can use Arcana.<br /> Some of the Changing Breeds, who are also half-spirit-half-flesh things can use Beast Magic.<br /> Interesting. Isn't it?<br /> <br /> (And yes, I know the book is bad, but that doesn't mean it never existed. It IS worth thinking about.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:54:20-07:00","id":856507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856405#post856405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so, for starters I'm working on statting up the Pangaeans Fox and Harvest, and some sample spirits. As noted before, these are all unofficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would it take to convince you to write up Mountain, possibly with some story seeds for modern day Mountain Hosts?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"