//goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:13:20-07:00","id":856520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856493#post856493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall from the Summoners book something about <i>things</i> still living in the Gauntlet itself. How do these things tie together?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Hell, per the City of the Moon story hook, it's possible there's an entire city in there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856507#post856507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would it take to convince you to write up Mountain, possibly with some story seeds for modern day Mountain Hosts?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> It would take quite a bit to convince me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Doing Mountain justice will be a fairly hefty endeavour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:16:23-07:00","id":856523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856520#post856520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would take quite a bit to convince me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Doing Mountain justice will be a fairly hefty endeavour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Any chance we might see Mountain Hosts in any upcoming Werewolf books? They sound big, tough and terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:19:55-07:00","id":856527,"title":"","content":"Dunno - that'd very much be Stew's remit and depends on what books are upcoming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:24:40-07:00","id":856534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856527#post856527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno - that'd very much be Stew's remit and depends on what books are upcoming!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How did Stew feel about you and Dave mucking about with Werewolf history and cosmology? Was he a little tentative or cackling mad and enthusiastic about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:44:00-07:00","id":856542,"title":"","content":"Definitely Cackling Mad and Enthusiastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:05:17-07:00","id":856559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856253#post856253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A later section also refers to werewolves as &quot;Native Predators&quot; of Pangaea. This also makes sense: as half-flesh, half-spirit creatures, a realm that blends both seems perfect for werewolves. Distinct from their progenitor god, different from the Hosts, werewolves seem better adapted for the duality. Perhaps their grounding in mortal flesh gives them that edge, or allowed them to adapt to a changing world. And these make for interesting theories and possibilities. What makes werewolves different? Why did they survive?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> After reading this, I came up with a possible answer to this question: I'm wondering if we can toss in an anthropological element to help explain why werewolves are distinct among Pangaeans, and to help keep werewolves at least tangentially close to humanity. I guess the way it would work in my head is that in some point in prehistory, Wolf noticed either a tribe of early humans who had domesticated wolves to assist them on the hunt. Wolf, maybe impressed with these humans working with his lesser kin, or maybe following the advice of her lover Moon who saw the potential these humans could add to Wolf's pack, worked together to basically adopt, modify, and guide the evolution of these humans into what we know as Werewolves.<br /> <br /> The initial humans probably loved this idea, since when THE Predator-God asks you to be his child, you say YES. I guess this could mean that the Wolf-Blooded actually came first, and the firstborn Werewolves were the first to go through their first change and thus fully embodied the three parts of themselves: the intelligence of Human, the theme and role of Wolf, and the renown of Moon. After that change, they transition from weird followers to the native hunters of Pangaea.<br /> <br /> But yea, this is why I think Werewolves are distinct from the other hosts, including the Adarusharu Wolf-Hosts: conceptually (which is what actually matters to spirits and Pangaeans) Werewolves are indeed the children of Wolf and Moon. In an evolutionary sense though, they're actually an offshoot of humanity and it's our species that now carries this legacy in that we provide the core symbol-creature that makes werewolves work.<br /> <br /> In any case, I also want to express my thanks to all the writers involved for making such a kick-ass section! Thank you so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","user":"The Lone Gunman","date":". 03-31-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:59:08-07:00","id":856599,"title":"","content":"So, strange connection just hit me. Awhawhiro, The Maelstrom rips the spirit of werewolves to shreds, it disrupts the God-Machine and Thrysus magic goes wild. If anywhere in the Fallen World is connected to Pangea, and Urfarah, New Zealand and the Awhawhiro seems like the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:52:18-07:00","id":856802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856599#post856599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, strange connection just hit me. Awhawhiro, The Maelstrom rips the spirit of werewolves to shreds, it disrupts the God-Machine and Thrysus magic goes wild. If anywhere in the Fallen World is connected to Pangea, and Urfarah, New Zealand and the Awhawhiro seems like the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I don't recall that. Where do you find it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:24:35-07:00","id":856820,"title":"","content":"God's Own Country, New Zealand Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:24:57-07:00","id":856896,"title":"","content":"So, I suppose from earlier mentions of the hearts of Bull and Wolf that Pangaean hearts can be split into pieces and retain their power? Do Omphalii have any powers beyond making an area a super-demense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:18:18-07:00","id":856928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856244#post856244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... Not so much. The strix aren't ephemera, but they're not really solid either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, yeah, a tenuous connection, but the Strix are described as 'like spirits but naturally material' unlike spirits which are naturally immaterial. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:56:42-07:00","id":857029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=856928#post856928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehh, yeah, a tenuous connection, but the Strix are described as 'like spirits but naturally material' unlike spirits which are naturally immaterial. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As much material consistency as smoke, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T02:54:00-07:00","id":857040,"title":"","content":"Material nonetheless. And as it was pointed out in other thread (there are like 3 or so about this era, which shows how awesome and popular it is) the creatures like Zmai, or the Breath from the end of the Predators book make excelent candidates to be or have been Pangaeans. One of them is also gaseous, material doesn't mean &quot;solid&quot; I can imagine an Ocean Pangaean being liquid, for example","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T03:50:17-07:00","id":857048,"title":"","content":"The only problem with strix being pangaean is that the place they come from still exists, and they can go back there if they want once they get powerful enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T04:45:05-07:00","id":857056,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that the Azlu, at least, are said to be able to build nests in the fabric of the Gauntlet itself. They're even &quot;spinning web-bridges to somewhere the Uratha cannot go.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to say there were other references to things that lived within the Gauntlet itself, but I can't remember where they were. That implies ... well, something strange, at any rate. Perhaps Pangaea was simply condensed into a super-thin spiritual barrier, and might somehow be expanded again. Or maybe there's something else at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T04:46:21-07:00","id":857057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857048#post857048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with strix being pangaean is that the place they come from still exists, and they can go back there if they want once they get powerful enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose like the Firstborn they could have found a new home. If you want to go the Pangaean route for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857056#post857056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to consider is that the Azlu, at least, are said to be able to build nests in the fabric of the Gauntlet itself. They're even &quot;spinning web-bridges to somewhere the Uratha cannot go.&quot;<br /> <br /> I want to say there were other references to things that lived within the Gauntlet itself, but I can't remember where they were. That implies ... well, something strange, at any rate. Perhaps Pangaea was simply condensed into a super-thin spiritual barrier, and might somehow be expanded again. Or maybe there's something else at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's these magical trilobites things that seem to be working at the ragged edges of the Gauntlet in one of the mage books. I think I tracked down mention of others, actually in the second edition core for Werewolf under the Gauntlet, it mentions tales of encountering spirits and corpses and 'other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2016, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:54:14-07:00","id":857100,"title":"","content":"There are a few hints towards that in Werewolf 2e as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe Father Wolf's death didn't cause Pangaea to immediately collapse. Maybe it just left Rat's spawn unchallenged in their endeavor to gnaw it down to almost nothing, and Spider's spawn to fill what was left of it with their webs. Hell, they might even have been aided by the Mourners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T06:57:03-07:00","id":857103,"title":"","content":"If you go with the idea that Father Wolf created Pangaea, and it went away with them, it's possible that no one was powerful enough in his absence to make something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:11:58-07:00","id":857160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857056#post857056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to say there were other references to things that lived within the Gauntlet itself, but I can't remember where they were. That implies ... well, something strange, at any rate. Perhaps Pangaea was simply condensed into a super-thin spiritual barrier, and might somehow be expanded again. Or maybe there's something else at work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The references you recall are the small, fragile and seemingly harmless organisms that live in the Gauntlet from the Mage supplement, Summoners, pp. 61-62.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:17:33-07:00","id":857164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857160#post857160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The references you recall are the small, fragile and seemingly harmless organisms that live in the Gauntlet from the Mage supplement, Summoners, pp. 61-62.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'm pretty sure she was talking about this quote on page 72 of Werewolf 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Uratha tell tales about encountering bizarre entities inside the Gauntlet \u2014 ghostly \u201cspirits,\u201d unnatural corpses of no known creature, splashes of blood, and other signs that the barrier is somehow inhabited, always just on the edge of the paralyzed traveler\u2019s senses. Some Cahalith say that when the Sundering rent the Border Marches apart, anything trapped inside was changed as well. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-01-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:25:17-07:00","id":857167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857164#post857164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I'm pretty sure she was talking about this quote on page 72 of Werewolf 2e.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Possibly. Summoners is still interesting in that it actually provides some depth and even stats to the Gauntlet creatures.<br /> <br /> Dave and Stew definitely need to further explore the Gauntlet ecology and cosmology in upcoming Mage and Werewolf supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:44:24-07:00","id":857321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857057#post857057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose like the Firstborn they could have found a new home. If you want to go the Pangaean route for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>With influences like they have they can literally create whole Amazon-sized places-that-arent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:59:25-07:00","id":857568,"title":"","content":"Pockets of hidden reality where Pangaea still exists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:44:37-07:00","id":857671,"title":"","content":"So, as promised, an initial draft of Fox's stats. Note that these are NOT official, have NOT been playtested and are the results of me noodling about a bit this afternoon. This is also obviously written prior to the Wise killing her and cracking her heart open.<br /> <br /> Also, prepare for weirdness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>FOX</b></span><br /> \u200bOf the Vinca pantheon, Fox is one of the least of the gods. It is not that the Vinca do not *respect* her so much as that their lives have little reason to fall under her attention. She is generally seen as the goddess of small predators, both benign and malign; villagers leave offerings out to foxes and venerate her so that their own small or youngest livestock will not be attacked by foxes, and so that little predators will help scour the area of vermin that might gnaw at crops. She is also respected for her supposed wisdom, and for her association with the colour red: if at all possible, ceramics and objects depicting her are coloured as red as possible with what is available, such as coloured earths.<br /> <br /> Fox is massive and horrifying in appearance. Much of her shape is as a fox would appear, albeit of huge aspect, but there is much that is wrong and alien about her appearance. Her shape, especially her head, sometimes possess strange, straight lines and abnormal angles that make her seem more like the *impression* of a fox drawn into the world; sometimes she has many heads, and sometimes she has no head at all while eyes open all along her limbs and flanks. Her claws and fangs are jagged and incredibly sharp, but Fox does not like to use them; using her natural weapons forces her to act on certain compulsions that she would rather not be chained to. She likes eating human viscera, although she does not like killing to get it; Fox prefers willing sacrifices, sometimes offering a blessing or great wisdom to a beneficiary that the sacrifice cares for in return for their offering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fox, Vermillion and Wise</b></span><br /> Rank 5 Pangaean<br /> Power 14 Finesse 15 Resistance 13<br /> Willpower 10 Essence 50<br /> Initiative 28 Defence 14 Speed 38<br /> Size 15 Corpus 28<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Foxes 5, Wisdom 3<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Drain, Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Innocuous, Regenerate, Speed<br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Mind 5<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Fox <b>must</b> offer audience and refrain from hostility to anyone who comes to her wearing red, although she is not bound further if the offer of audience is refused or if the visitor acts against her.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A weapon crafted with bone taken from three hundred and thirty three different foxes.<br /> <br /> <i>Divine Bleed:</i> The first time in a scene that she suffers Corpus damage, Fox may reflexively use the Awe, Dement, Emotional Aura or Hallucination Numina for free. She may also use the Create power of her Influence (Foxes) for free each time she suffers damage, or she may create a Rank 1 fox spirit instead.<br /> <br /> <i>Eye-Snatcher:</i> Fox's melee attacks inflict the Blind tilt on victims.<br /> <br /> <i>Foxfires:</i> Wherever Fox touches living plant matter, she leaves strange patches of fungus that glow with ephemeral light. These fungi have two effects: their illumination reveals anything nearby that is in Twilight, and Fox herself can perceive anything within the radius of their light. If Fox is killed, all foxfire fungus immediately catches fire and burns for at least an hour with the intensity of a bonfire. Once created, foxfire fungus has a natural lifespan and will eventually die off.<br /> <br /> <i>Lord of Foxes: </i>Fox is aware of the health and emotional state (basic information like fear, pain, hunger, etc) of all foxes within three hundred and thirty three miles of her location. If there are no foxes within that area, she suffers a -3 penalty to all of her Attributes. By touching a dead or incapacitated human, Fox can cause a number of newly-created foxes equal to the human's Stamina to tear their way out of the body and into existence.<br /> <br /> <i>Many Shapes:</i> Fox has four different shapes, all of which possess the same attributes and abilities and which it costs nothing for her to shift to. As well as her large, true shape, Fox can take the form of a normal fox, a normal human, or an otherworldly blend of human and divine fox. Suffering damage in any of these three forms immediately forces her back into her true form. She may also dissolve her true form into a swarm of normal foxes by spending 10 Essence and 2 Willpower points, only one of which is the Pangaean herself; however, for three minutes and thirty three seconds, all of the foxes created in this way appear to be the Pangaean to any supernatural senses and forms of detection.<br /> <br /> <i>Monstrous Form:</i> Fox has Armour 13, and may spend 1 Essence to shrug off any Tilt she experiences. These benefits do not apply to attacks from her Banes.<br /> <br /> <i>Overwhelming Presence:</i> A mortal human who encounters Fox suffers an Integrity breaking point. If this roll is failed, the character gains the Madness persistent condition.<br /> <br /> <i>Red Shift:</i> Attempts to fold space or tamper with the fabric of time that target Fox or affect an area she can physically perceive (including appropriate uses of the Space and Time Arcana) allow Fox to pre-emptively and reflexively change her location by up to three hundred and thirty three miles. This is not actual teleportation, simply the nature of reality correcting itself. If Fox is in the presence of someone using a supernatural power to move forward or backwards in time, or to stop time, the Pangaean may spend 1 point of Willpower to 'tag along' if she wishes, allowing her to arrive at the same point in time or, for example, act normally along with the power's user if they have stopped time.<br /> <br /> <i>Visceral Sacrament:</i> If Fox kills or incapacitates a human character with her melee attacks, she must spend one round consuming the (soon-to-be) corpse's viscera. This grants her 1 point of Willpower and 5 points of Essence.<br /> <br /> <i>Vulpine Rapture:</i> Fox may reflexively cause up to three foxes or Rank 1 fox spirits in her presence each turn to tear themselves apart in a spasm of flesh, spirit and light; she may immediately use the Rapture numen (which she does not normally have access to) against one target for each fox or spirit sacrificed in this way.<br /> <br /> <i>Wisdom-Eater:</i> Whenever a character succeeds at a roll based on Intelligence, Academics or Occult while in the presence of Fox, the Pangaean gains 1 point of Essence. Fox may, if she chooses, also strip the character of a single point of Essence or Mana in the process. If Fox spends 1 Willpower point, she may also initiate a Clash of Wills against the character whereupon, if she is successful, she may tear their soul out and reflexively consume it, giving her the rote quality on her next use of the Mind Arcanum. Upon going to sleep, Fox may spend 1 Willpower point extend the range on this effect for up to three hundred and thirty three miles rather than just her presence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":37}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:54:22-07:00","id":857676,"title":"","content":"Expect weirdness indeed...<br /> <br /> EDIT: I love it, so you know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T07:01:23-07:00","id":857680,"title":"","content":"Fox!! Aw dayum, that is weird and cool as heck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/