orum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:46:02-07:00","id":857757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857754#post857754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't Fox have 5 arcana dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has Mind 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:04:05-07:00","id":857766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857729#post857729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is one of the Lowest Gods. By Urfarah, how did those Mages win...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to believe they did it by being sneaky, underhanded, and well-informed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:12:36-07:00","id":857771,"title":"","content":"Finished reading Fox, she's everything I hoped she'd be.<br /> <br /> Now to figure out what I'm going to do with this information, considering she's the first casualty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:15:15-07:00","id":857775,"title":"","content":"When I reached the <i>Wisdom-Eate</i><i>r</i> in her write-up, Fox went from being terrifying to being just plain unfair.<br /> <br /> Also, I know it's not intended, but I noticed that her metaphysics acknowledge the imperial system of measurement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:19:12-07:00","id":857779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857775#post857775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I know it's not intended, but I noticed that her metaphysics acknowledge the imperial system of measurement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... What do you think might make a good alternative? Cubits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:30:44-07:00","id":857784,"title":"","content":"Her length from tail to nose, the length of her pounce, the distance She can run in 333 heartbeats. In almost all circumstances the measurement system would be irrelevant but in Fox's case the number 333 is mystically relevant. If you take the range of her powers and divide it by 333 you get... an arbitrary length that won't mean anything for thousands of years. Unless, at some point in the future her heart falls into the hands of occult cartographers.<br /> <br /> Still, nitpicking. I love the write-up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just read up how ancient cubits are. I thought you were just kidding. Now I think you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 04-02-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:39:54-07:00","id":857789,"title":"","content":"Fox is the Vermilion Wisdom. Who is to say the lore she caries does not reach to times that she does not?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I had an interesting thought. What about modern shapeshifters born when someone with the potential to be a Werewolf or Werebull or whatever stumbles across one of the lost God Hearts? Heck, maybe these people even hear strange whispers of the dead Pangean's dread dreams that call them to act in a way that could eventually allow their maker to be restored in a new form?<br /> <br /> At least, it might make a neat Mystery Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:42:41-07:00","id":857791,"title":"","content":"Since the omphalos may be a part of a Pangaean soul, an idigam might be able to shove one into a person or werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:50:30-07:00","id":857796,"title":"","content":"Fox can explicitly hitch a ride on time/space warpings. There's your cue to include it on your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:53:44-07:00","id":857800,"title":"","content":"Not to argue fixed points at all, but her death is something of an instigating point for Mages(and vicariously, the Uratha). If I were doing a time travel game, that'd happen, but in a historical game, not so much.<br /> <br /> Of course, one of the neat things about horror urban fantasy is that time travel can often be introduced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:12:00-07:00","id":857811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857784#post857784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I just read up how ancient cubits are. I thought you were just kidding. Now I think you're right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry, I suppose that might have come off sounding cheeky, but I meant it as a serious suggestion. Though, 333 cubits would significantly shorten the range as compared to 333 miles. Maybe 3,333 cubits would be better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:28:16-07:00","id":857821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857729#post857729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is one of the Lowest Gods. By Urfarah, how did those Mages win...</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bFox is one of the lowest of the Vinca pantheon, but note that there were other Pangaeans as well. Some were 'only' Rank 3 or 4, although those would have been less worthwhile prey for the Wise as their hearts would not have gone nearly so far in providing omphalos stones for settlements (I imagine Rank 3 and 4 could only provide a single stone, but I reserve the right to change this view at any point in the future on a whim).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857730#post857730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, you really got a lot of milage out of that &quot;Many Pangaeans also possess other unique powers over the world&quot; line!<br /> <br /> Also, I love Fox so much! I'm definitely going to have to find an excuse to use it in a game some time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, the unique powers are where Pangaeans should express a lot of their unusual nature.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:40:27-07:00","id":857829,"title":"","content":"I can see the problem. 3,333 cubits are still less than a mile (or so Google tells me), but 333,000 cubits are 94.6 of a mile, so closer in our ballpark. However, in the write-up 333 shows up both in Her power range and in Her Bane. Changing one but not the other makes it far less elegant and killing 333,000 foxes feels excessive. I think if there ever was a setting in which more folk-tale based measurements could be used, it's this one. Hence, my suggestions of &quot;the length of Her pounce&quot; and such. Ultimately if it's worth changing, it's Acrozatarim's call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:58:48-07:00","id":857903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857160#post857160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The references you recall are the small, fragile and seemingly harmless organisms that live in the Gauntlet from the Mage supplement, Summoners, pp. 61-62.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857164#post857164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'm pretty sure she was talking about this quote on page 72 of Werewolf 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, there is a type of Iris that leads mages into the Gauntlet itself. They become compressed and the world outside is all huge and distorted. Lends perhaps further credence to the idea that the Gauntlet is like a super-dense collapsed Pangaea, which makes one wonder if the process can be reversed....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:07:54-07:00","id":857909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857903#post857903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, there is a type of Iris that leads mages into the Gauntlet itself. They become compressed and the world outside is all huge and distorted. Lends perhaps further credence to the idea that the Gauntlet is like a super-dense collapsed Pangaea, which makes one wonder if the process can be reversed....</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this referenced?<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries? Mage 2e? Somewhere in Dark Eras?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:14:33-07:00","id":857916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857909#post857909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this referenced?<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries? Mage 2e? Somewhere in Dark Eras?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2E. Which, I feel pretty confident, will blow your mind with how awesome it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:25:29-07:00","id":857920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857916#post857916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage 2E. Which, I feel pretty confident, will blow your mind with how awesome it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Citing Mage 2e before its release is both cheating and cruel. <br /> <br /> Did you write the pertinent 2e material? Have the small fishy creatures living in the Gauntlet from Summoners been retconned out of existence? <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I assume that the collapse of Pangaea can be reversed by simply finding Father Wolf's soul shards and reuniting them with his carcass in the First Wound. Piece of cake...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:55:26-07:00","id":857943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857920#post857920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Citing Mage 2e before its release is both cheating and cruel.<br /> <br /> Did you write the pertinent 2e material? Have the small fishy creatures living in the Gauntlet from Summoners been retconned out of existence?<br /> <br /> Also, I assume that the collapse of Pangaea can be reversed by simply finding Father Wolf's soul shards and reuniting them with his carcass in the First Wound. Piece of cake...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't write it. To be fair, it's just one sentence of a paragraph in the section about Irises, but it's a cool one with a lot of story implications. The Vergelings from Summoners are still a thing, so far as I know, and I intend to use them myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:01:44-07:00","id":858013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857757#post857757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has Mind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aparantly blind. I only just now saw it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:25:50-07:00","id":858024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=858013#post858013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aparantly blind. I only just now saw it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind 5 working as intended... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:26:26-07:00","id":858025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=858013#post858013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aparantly blind. I only just now saw it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot judge you, it took me multiple reads to notice that too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:36:39-07:00","id":858028,"title":"","content":"The book said that they can be as 'weak' as rank 3 and I'm wondering what such an entity would seem like and how their Omphalos Stones would manifest differently than stronger pangaeans? Also anything 'rumor' worthy for what the Great Predator's Omphalos Stone would be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:48:53-07:00","id":858038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faster-Than-FedEx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=858028#post858028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book said that they can be as 'weak' as rank 3 and I'm wondering what such an entity would seem like and how their Omphalos Stones would manifest differently than stronger pangaeans? Also anything 'rumor' worthy for what the Great Predator's Omphalos Stone would be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible the higher the rank the more shards a soul can have. Bull and Bird gifted parts of their souls and were still out and about.<br /> <br /> As for Mother Wolf, I can't think of any stones that really resonate with the idea, but considering the section was written after the last book to have come out related to Werewolf or Mage there might not be anything 'official.' If there's rumors when the Pack comes out I'm sure there will be posts about it.<br /> <br /> There might not be an omphalos stone, depending on how Mother Wolf was killed. In a battle with the Firstborn and Uratha versus the First Pack and their progenitor and who knows what else it may have been destroyed. But I wouldn't expect that to be stated, as the idea of it is too good a plot hook to really block off like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-02-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:24:54-07:00","id":858105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857671#post857671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FOX<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:17:35-07:00","id":858235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=858038#post858038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible the higher the rank the more shards a soul can have. Bull and Bird gifted parts of their souls and were still out and about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that many supernatural's power stats basically symbolize, how much of their soul's potential was realized. Blood Potency, Wyrd and especially Gnosis. What the Bull and Bird did amounts to essentially creating Soul Stones. It probably lowered their powers present in their own bodies a bit, but they can normally move around like mages can. I would rule the amount of shards they can create to be their Rank x2 (Gnosis 5 mage really doesn't equal in power to a rank 5 Pangean. Gnosis 10 mage on the other hand...), maybe adding -1 representing the shard that has to stay in them so that they can exist. The -1 wouldnt apply if the heart is taken unvoluntarily from a dead Pangean, naturally.<br /> <br /> This made me realize, maybe the mages (Hollow Keepers) *did* learn how to create Soul Stones thanks to observing the shards/act of their severing and Omphalos hearts. Bull's children apparently made a Legacy by understanding Bull's Omphalos stones, so why not? Also, if the shards are like Soul Stones... delicious, delicious Sympathy for casting spells on the Pangean that granted them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 04-03-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T11:37:33-07:00","id":858422,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why I was surprised at how horrifying Fox is physically, considering how the two great Hosts' progenitors have always been described (to say nothing of Bull's incidentally-mentioned ten-thousand hooves).<br /> <br /> Though now I'm wondering what more abstract Pangaeans like Harvest and the seasonal divinities looked like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:43:19-07:00","id":858458,"title":"","content":"Suddenly, the corrupted visage of Violence Maeltinents taking the assumed form of Urfarah complete with chainsaw-like teeth doesn't seems so out of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:59:40-07:00","id":858465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=858458#post858458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suddenly, the corrupted visage of Violence Maeltinents taking the assumed form of Urfarah complete with chainsaw-like teeth doesn't seems so out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto the False Father's &quot;improvements.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:17:37-07:00","id":859687,"title":"","content":"As before with Fox, this is unofficial, it is first draft, and it is subject to change or disavowment as per my whims. So here's Harvest, a lower-ranking Pangaean:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>HARVEST</b></span><br /> <br /> \u200bHarvest is a Pangaean of autumn, a shambling divinity of the plentifulness and the hunger that follows the growing season - the time when animals run fat with the bounty from which they feed, and when all must look to eat their fill before the coming of winter. Harvest is not the agricultural, pastoral gathering of the world under humankind but rather the natural cycle which that emerges from. Harvest is always, always hungry.<br /> <br /> The Pangaean resembles no known animal. It is huge, so large as to shatter trees then gnaw on their splintered trunks. Powerful, elephantine legs support Harvest's immense bulk, while wiry and surprisingly deft limbs sprout from her front and flanks. Her maw is a forest of mandibles, slicing pincers, fangs, talons, hooks and scissoring blades of bone that meticulously disassemble anything the divinity decides to try and eat. This is not a swift process. Harvest is always hungry, but she is always painstaking in her meals when she has the luxury of time; her thousand-toothed mouth works with methodical effort to strip the food to pieces, layer by layer, piece by piece, seperating all the different parts and substances so that they can be best made use of in the divine fires of her gut. She pays no heed to the state of her food; a human caught in Harvest's maw will die over agonising hours as they find themselves slowly, cautiously pulled apart. The maw and head, wide like the hood of a cobra, also play host to Harvest's many eyes; large, surprisingly human and thoughtful. The features of her head and her carapaced back are strangely abstract, almost ephemeral compared to the brutal physicality of her mouth; dangling tendrils and fungus-like growths emit a soft luminescence and form a matted tangled cloak over the carapace.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Harvest, Watchful and Ravenous</b></span><br /> Rank 4 Pangaean<br /> Power 12 Finesse 10 Resistance 12<br /> Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> Initiative 22 Defence 12 Speed 25<br /> Size 20 Corpus 32<br /> <br /> <b>Influences: </b>Hunger 4, Foraging 2<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Entropic Decay, Hallucination, Rapture, Regenerate, Stalwart<br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Matter 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Harvest must offer audience and refrain from hostility to anyone who comes to her bearing a gift of food, although she is not bound further if the offer of audience is refused or if the visitor acts against her.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> The names of 44 humans from the same community who all died of starvation, carved or inscribed into something; the created talisman or weapon only retains power for 44 days after the death of the last of the starving humans.<br /> <br /> <i>Bountiful Presence:</i> Any plant or animal (including humans) that enters Harvest's presence is touched by the Pangaean's power. Consuming the fruits, grains or flesh from such living beings within 44 days of Harvest's presence has several beneficial effects on the consumer \u2013 their hunger is completely sated and, for 44 days, they heal at twice the normal rate and can go for twice the usual time without food and without water before starting to suffer damage from either lack.<br /> <i>Divine Bleed:</i> The first time in a scene that she suffers Corpus damage, Harvest may reflexively use the Awe, Dement, Hallucination or Rapture Numina for free. Any time she suffers damage, Harvest may reflexively use her Influence (Hunger) for free or cause a harvestman to form from the ichors that splash on the ground.<br /> <i>Harvester:</i> Harvest is immune to any form of poison, venom, toxin, befoulment, curse or supernatural effect that she would suffer from eating something (including via a grapple). When a victim in her grapple is killed, Harvest gains 5 Essence and the ability to inflict any sort of poison, toxin, curse etc that might have been resident in the victim's flesh through her own melee attacks. Such harvested powers remain available to Harvest for 44 minutes, or 44 days in the case of a supernatural victim.<br /> <i>Monstrous Form:</i> Harvest has Armour 12, and may spend 1 Essence to shrug off any Tilt she experiences. These benefits do not apply to attacks from her Banes.<br /> <i>Overwhelming Presence:</i> A mortal human who encounters Harvest suffers an Integrity breaking point. If this roll is failed, the character gains the Madness persistent condition.<br /> <i>Seer of All:</i> Harvest can detect lies and see through illusions perfectly; she is completely aware of the true nature and location of everything within 44 yards of her. She can never be surprised or ambushed. Whenever a character succeeds at a perception check within Harvest's presence, the Pangaean gains 1 point of Essence; she may spend 1 point of Willpower to immediately gain access to all of that character's memories for 44 days. For any character whom she has access to the memories of in this way, Harvest may manifest directly in their Oneiros if she meditates into the Astral, from wherein she may harvest and consume their Oneiros and everything in it to refill her Willpower and Essence pools over a period of 44 minutes.<br /> <i>Vivisect:</i> Harvest benefits from the rote quality on grapple checks, and on a successful grapple may inflict one point of aggravated damage and a persistent Arm Wrack, Blinded or Leg Wrack Tilt on her opponent as well as the usual effects of succeeding. When inflicting damage with a grapple, Harvest' attacks have 5 points of armour piercing and ignore 5 points of durability.<br /> <br /> The spirit fragments hewn from Harvest's flesh come in a myriad of shapes, each reflecting a facet of their mistress-mother's thoughts or nature. Sometimes they are spindly-legged spiders with shredding mouths like the Pangaean's; sometimes they are tottering things of thorny stems and oozing meat with claws that grasp and tear. They skitter and scuttle in search of meals to bring back home with them, whereupon they press into Harvest's flesh until it puckers with teeth and grasping hands to pull them back within with a bloody, rending embrace. Although spirits, harvestmen are always materialised.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Harvestman</span></b><br /> Rank 1 spirit<br /> Power 2 Finesse 4 Resistance 2<br /> Willpower 6 Essence 10<br /> Initiative 6 Defence 4 Speed 16<br /> Size 4 Corpus 6<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Hunger 1<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Drain, Harvest, Speed<br /> <i>Harvest:</i> The harvestman's attacks have 2 points of armour piercing and ignore 2 points of durability. The harvestman may spend 1 Essence to make any Arm Wrack, Blinded or Leg Wrack Tilt it inflicts persistent, removing the relevant body part from the victim; if the harvestman can make it back to Harvest, it is reabsorbed into her and she regains 5 Essence and 1 point of Willpower.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":32}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:57:36-07:00","id":859793,"title":"","content":"That's... wow. My god. Between Harvest and Fox I don't think I want to contemplate a Rank 6+ Pangaean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:19:02-07:00","id":859829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857821#post857821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bFox is one of the lowest of the Vinca pantheon, but note that there were other Pangaeans as well. Some were 'only' Rank 3 or 4, although those would have been less worthwhile prey for the Wise as their hearts would not have gone nearly so far in providing omphalos stones for settlements (I imagine Rank 3 and 4 could only provide a single stone, but I reserve the right to change this view at any point in the future on a whim).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, the unique powers are where Pangaeans should express a lot of their unusual nature.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,speaking bout unique powers,does anybody have theories about why exactly the pangeans have arcana,? Mine is that the when the Fall happenned and the Time Before was ended,some supernal beings,even supernal <i>gods </i>decides to give a some of their power to pangeans because the pangeans had a better chance of surviving the fall,since they're not on the exarchs shit-list","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-05-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:29:53-07:00","id":859836,"title":"","content":"Naturally attuned to the supernal, Awakenings not necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:35:06-07:00","id":859842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859829#post859829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh,speaking bout unique powers,does anybody have theories about why exactly the pangeans have arcana,? Mine is that the when the Fall happenned and the Time Before was ended,some supernal beings,even supernal <i>gods </i>decides to give a some of their power to pangeans because the pangeans had a better chance of surviving the fall,since they're not on the exarchs shit-list</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The theory of Pangaeans as fallen Supernal Gods is explicitly referenced in Dark Eras, p. 58,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Though similar to spirits, Pangaeans are \u2014 along with werewolves \u2014 the true natives of the Border Marches. They are powerful symbols of natural cycles and forces, the gods of weather, the seasons, and the animals. Unlike spirits, they are not reflections of the world but pillars of it \u2014 primeval divinities born in this rift between worlds. Each Pangaean possesses colossal power, and the Wise believe such an entity may even be a fallen inhabitant of the Supernal World, trapped between Flesh and Shadow by the end of the Time Before&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:36:31-07:00","id":859843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859842#post859842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The theory of Pangaeans as fallen Supernal Gods is explicitly referenced in Dark Eras, p. 58,<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>my mistake,i totallty forgot that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T13:49:45-07:00","id":859849,"title":"","content":"So maybe the Pangeans are the result of refuges from the Primal Wild adjusting to fit more naturally in a place that resonated with them? <br /> <br /> If so, I wonder if beings from other &quot;places&quot;* in the Supernal did the same. For example, beings from Pandemonium wpuld likdly be capable of adapting to a place where thought is the guiding principle and where distance is based more on sympathy and association than the laws of physics... which, come to think of it, does describe the Astral...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:19:18-07:00","id":859867,"title":"","content":"Oh dear, that's a frightening idea. What if that's where the first Huntsmen, Hobgoblins, and True Fae came from?<br /> <br /> Better question- does Pangaea sort of bleed into the Hedge, or vice-versa?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:45:24-07:00","id":859891,"title":"","content":"So out of curiosity, how does Harvest deal with or co-exist with the Hunger spirits detailed in the sidebar at the beginning of the chapter? The Pangean section didn't mention much on how they interact with Spirits IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:46:38-07:00","id":859894,"title":"","content":"Harvest is... uniquely terrifying in her hunger. I am really fond of how distinctly the appearance and inclinations of Harvest reflect her era and its brutality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:57:38-07:00","id":859902,"title":"","content":"While I believe the Pangaeans were an excellent addition to the setting and well written and fun, I'm not enamored with their Supernal origin, even if stated only as a theory.<br /> <br /> Since Pangaean Hearts are effectively Supernal Soul Stones that create super-demesnes and Pangaeans have easy access to the Astral Relams, the Supernal origin &quot;theory&quot; has ample evidence to establish it as setting fact. I prefer a much more clearly contained Mage cosmology. More importantly, having a (partial) Supernal origin for much of the Werewolf mythos encourages Mage critics and their recent &quot;mage supremacy&quot; complaints. Werewolf: The Forsaken has a rich enough history that it didn't need to include mages and the Supernal, even when crossover is encouraged.<br /> <br /> I was particularly surprised this was included after Dave recently made the point of emphasizing in his Signs of Sorcery spoilers how little in the general CofD setting was intentionally not the direct result of Supernal shenanigans. Although I understand and appreciate theories about how most other realms, inhabitants and even splats are Supernal in origin or nature, the material in The Sundering World strongly encourages these speculations, exactly the type of situation Dave seemed to want to avoid (*cough* Supernal Arcadia vs. Changeling Arcadia *cough*).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:08:06-07:00","id":859910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859894#post859894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harvest is... uniquely terrifying in her hunger. I am really fond of how distinctly the appearance and inclinations of Harvest reflect her era and its brutality.</div> </div> </div> </div>If she still around Beasts would be all over her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:09:16-07:00","id":859912,"title":"","content":"While I haven't read the chapters myself, it's my interpretation that the Arcana that Pangeans display is less of a literal supernal equivalent and more like something of a super influence abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:11:15-07:00","id":859917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859902#post859902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I believe the Pangaeans were an excellent addition to the setting and well written and fun, I'm not enamored with their Supernal origin, even if stated only as a theory.<br /> <br /> Since Pangaean Hearts are effectively Supernal Soul Stones that create super-demesnes and Pangaeans have easy access to the Astral Relams, the Supernal origin &quot;theory&quot; has ample evidence to establish it as setting fact. I prefer a much more clearly contained Mage cosmology. More importantly, having a (partial) Supernal origin for much of the Werewolf mythos encourages Mage critics and their recent &quot;mage supremacy&quot; complaints. Werewolf: The Forsaken has a rich enough history that it didn't need to include mages and the Supernal, even when crossover is encouraged.<br /> <br /> I was particularly surprised this was included after Dave recently made the point of emphasizing in his Signs of Sorcery spoilers how little in the general CofD setting was intentionally not the direct result of Supernal shenanigans. Although I understand and appreciate theories about how most other realms, inhabitants and even splats are Supernal in origin or nature, the material in The Sundering World strongly encourages these speculations, exactly the type of situation Dave seemed to want to avoid (*cough* Supernal Arcadia vs. Changeling Arcadia *cough*).</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this notion, given that humans can do all these things as mages, and humans are decidedly non-Supernal. The examples we have seem to cast them as something like werewolf-like beings that happen to also be very mage like. Add in the comments about them being pillars of the world, and I argue that they have plenty of evidence to be the Fallen world. They might reach into the Supernal like mages, but honestly that just means they were the Fallen World's bridges in a fashion similar to some of the Old Gods for the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:15:02-07:00","id":859918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859902#post859902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I believe the Pangaeans were an excellent addition to the setting and well written and fun, I'm not enamored with their Supernal origin, even if stated only as a theory.<br /> <br /> Since Pangaean Hearts are effectively Supernal Soul Stones that create super-demesnes and Pangaeans have easy access to the Astral Relams, the Supernal origin &quot;theory&quot; has ample evidence to establish it as setting fact. I prefer a much more clearly contained Mage cosmology. More importantly, having a (partial) Supernal origin for much of the Werewolf mythos encourages Mage critics and their recent &quot;mage supremacy&quot; complaints. Werewolf: The Forsaken has a rich enough history that it didn't need to include mages and the Supernal, even when crossover is encouraged.<br /> <br /> I was particularly surprised this was included after Dave recently made the point of emphasizing in his Signs of Sorcery spoilers how little in the general CofD setting was intentionally not the direct result of Supernal shenanigans. Although I understand and appreciate theories about how most other realms, inhabitants and even splats are Supernal in origin or nature, the material in The Sundering World strongly encourages these speculations, exactly the type of situation Dave seemed to want to avoid (*cough* Supernal Arcadia vs. Changeling Arcadia *cough*).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still waiting for the book, so my opinion might be less valid. However, from what I've heard, I have the exact opposite feeling. Werewolf has a setting with very little space for variation on it's cosmology. The Hisil is real, Luna is real, everything that should be &quot;legend&quot; is real, not allowing for many creation hypothesis, reducing mystery to almost zero.<br /> <br /> I am extremely happy that the developers decided to add very weird twists to the main mythos. The Mother/Father Wolf was not a Spirit, it was something else. We don't have any proof that it was The Wolf that really spawned Uratha, since Wolf's bane is in fact the Bane of every other Pangaean. Silver was already a weakness, meaning that the Moon punishment legends are bullshit. Nothing is set in stone anymore, and now I can have very old Spirits, even Indigam, fuck with the minds of Uratha cahracters just by reavealing that their beliefs doesn't hold true. I could obviously do that before, by tearing up the cosmology, but now they really freed Werewolf Storytellers from the schackles that had been placed by &quot;Father Wolf / Urdaga / Anshega&quot; relationship and mythology.<br /> <br /> What is the problem if the Pangaeans were also able to identify the supernal symbols of their time? It could prove the exact opposite, that Werewolf Supremacy is true, since their might have been created by the most powerful Supernal God that ever walked the fallen world. I may even do Mage crossovers where Uratha characters discover how to protect themselves against Arcana by finding and studying the hearts of their old progenitors. What if Luna herself is a Pangaean that survived and only disguises as a spirit? If Uratha are native to the Border Marches, could their hearts be used as Soul Stones also?<br /> <br /> In the end, I feel happy that this new CofD cosmology seems to be touching everywhere, with several gamelines having reasons to interact. What is there was no Mother Wolf, but instead the Mother Horror of all beasts? What if Werewolves are limited Beasts that manifested out of the astral and need help to achieve their full potential?<br /> <br /> I don't know, it feels like a lot of fun to me. whichs<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, as described in this passage: &quot;<i>They are powerful symbols of natural cycles and forces&quot;,</i> which allows the interpretation that their use of Arcana derives from them being actual Symbols, the pillars of exitence. They define what &quot;Harvest&quot; means, and not the contrary, they are almost platonic ideals, if not totally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:29:48-07:00","id":859928,"title":"","content":"Also, if you were going to pick a chapter to introduce something that straddles and blurs the space between werewolf's neck of the woods and mage's cosmology...Well, never a better chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:52:20-07:00","id":859940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859928#post859928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you were going to pick a chapter to introduce something that straddles and blurs the space between werewolf's neck of the woods and mage's cosmology...Well, never a better chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I indicated in my comment here and elsewhere, as a fan of both Mage and Werewolf, I was overall very pleased with The Sundered World chapter and the rest of Dark Eras. Dave and Chris did a fantastic job. <br /> <br /> No doubt TSW would be the appropriate chapter to bridge Mage and Werewolf. However, given the historic and recent (and sometimes quite heated) complaints about Mage &quot;supremacy&quot; and cosmological intrusiveness into other gamelines (arguments I often disagree with quite strongly) and Dave's clear and unmistakable intent to limit the Supernal as the cause for much of the CofD's strangeness and horror both within Mage itself and setting crossovers (e.g., Arcadias, Signs of Sorcery spoilers, etc.), I was indeed surprised to see the Supernal so strongly implied to be part of the Uratha's actual origins. While superficially fun and definitely interesting, I believe it may ultimately prove distracting or contentious among a number of fans and renew, rather than settle, the setting arguments that the new editions sought to lay to rest.<br /> <br /> For instance, and certainly meaning absolutely no criticism or disrespect to Arcanist and others, the Werewolf Supernal origins are encouraging precisely the theorizing about connections between Supernal Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia and the Hedge that Dave wanted to end once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:55:25-07:00","id":859942,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's such a massive leap to go from the Wise theorizing about what the Pangeans <i>maybe </i>are to them having a supernal origin. Like, just because they can manipulate stuff with Arcana implies connection, but not really any kind of meaningful origin?<br /> <br /> And what meaningful origin is there in this situation anyway? All it would say is that the Pangeans were <i>maybe </i>around in The Time Before. What does that actually do or suggest for people to take issue with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:15:52-07:00","id":859956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859942#post859942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's such a massive leap to go from the Wise theorizing about what the Pangeans <i>maybe </i>are to them having a supernal origin. Like, just because they can manipulate stuff with Arcana implies connection, but not really any kind of meaningful origin?<br /> <br /> And what meaningful origin is there in this situation anyway? All it would say is that the Pangeans were <i>maybe </i>around in The Time Before. What does that actually do or suggest for people to take issue with?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are many fans who, rightly or wrongly, try to ascribe everything in the setting to Supernal origins or nature, and believe this somehow makes Mage the setting and mage characters &quot;supreme&quot; over other splats. This is often discussed on the OP forums and elsewhere. While I do not personally agree with this perspective or believe it particularly meaningful in running a chronicle even if true, many others certainly are not of the same mind on the topic. I also appreciate that many fans like the mythos of their preferred gamelines to be generally self-contained, no less when crossover is not a priority. In fact, Dave has intentionally tried to limit Supernal cosmological &quot;spillover,&quot; going as far to explicitly and very conclusively dealing with old arguments in Mage 2e like the lack of connection between Supernal and Changeling Arcadia.<br /> <br /> My criticism is certainly not that Dave and Chris didn't handle the topic or TSW in a creative and fun manner. Quite the opposite. I was simply surprised that the Werewolf supernal connection was so explicit instead of very vaguely or tangentially implied. If I was the Grand Poobah of The CofD and all its gamelines, I would have likely made a minor some changes here and there concerning this matter to forestall some potential problems and fan discontent. I fear my relatively minor criticism might be blown well out of proportion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:16:01-07:00","id":859957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859829#post859829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh,speaking bout unique powers,does anybody have theories about why exactly the pangeans have arcana,? Mine is that the when the Fall happenned and the Time Before was ended,some supernal beings,even supernal <i>gods </i>decides to give a some of their power to pangeans because the pangeans had a better chance of surviving the fall,since they're not on the exarchs shit-list</div> </div> </div> </div>I already stated mine. Pangaea doesn't just bridge the gap between flesh and shadow. It is, as its name suggests, all worlds. That includes the Supernal world. Pangaeans are creatures native to a place that is at once material, terminal, vital, spiritual, temporal, auspicious, spatial, mental, dynamic, and primal. They touch the symbolic truths behind reality as easily as they touch flesh, spirit, dreams, and (in my inrerpretation) narrative, afterlife, and perhaps even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-05-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:25:36-07:00","id":859960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859957#post859957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already stated mine. Pangaea doesn't just bridge the gap between flesh and shadow. It is, as its name suggests, all worlds. That includes the Supernal world. Pangaeans are creatures native to a place that is at once material, terminal, vital, spiritual, temporal, auspicious, spatial, mental, dynamic, and primal. They touch the symbolic truths behind reality as easily as they touch flesh, spirit, dreams, and (in my inrerpretation) narrative, afterlife, and perhaps even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>My third note in for my take on Neolithic Changeling is &quot;The world is a much smaller place.&quot; Arcadia's currently called the Dark Ocean.<br /> <br /> Fanon does not canon make, but make of the interpretation what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:30:14-07:00","id":859964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859960#post859960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My third note in for my take on Neolithic Changeling is &quot;The world is a much smaller place.&quot; Arcadia's currently called the Dark Ocean.<br /> <br /> Fanon does not canon make, but make of the interpretation what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div> Was it named by Whom in universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T17:12:44-07:00","id":859980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859964#post859964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it named by Whom in universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were inclined to anyone naming it, I reckon their name would far more likely be Wake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Zane</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">For he did not know, that beyond the lake he called home, there lied a deeper, and darker ocean green. Where waves are both wilder and more serene. To its ports I've been, to its ports I've been.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: And again, that's just fanon. Don't take me too seriously here as far as the extended conversation goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-05-2016, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:27:22-07:00","id":860022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859980#post859980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were inclined to anyone naming it, I reckon their name would far more likely be Wake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: And again, that's just fanon. Don't take me too seriously here as far as the extended conversation goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh never played that,sounds cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:16:49-07:00","id":860073,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &quot;universal&quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board? Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:23:36-07:00","id":860076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860073#post860073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &quot;universal&quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board? Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T20:25:17-07:00","id":860078,"title":"","content":"As a spirit of autumn, its existence is not quite universal, limited to latitude +/- 23.4 degrees or more. Then there are the things that feed all year round, which vastly outnumber the things that base around the seasons. It's the pillar for a more temporal concept.<br /> <br /> Whereas a fox is a fox, wherever it goes, whatever the season.<br /> <br /> Just a guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T21:27:32-07:00","id":860105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860073#post860073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &quot;universal&quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board? Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, consider the biggest one embodied the sheer concept of the Hunt in that period. Everything that wasn't plant or mineral lived or died by this concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T22:00:48-07:00","id":860123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860073#post860073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &amp;quot;universal&amp;quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board? Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well remember, Fox isn't just a representation of the concept of foxes - if that's all she was, she could be a spirit. Fox is the patron of all small predators including foxes, as well as an embodiment of wisdom, and symbol of the color red.<br /> <br /> Harvest is a symbol of autumn, and an embodiment of the act of reaping earth's bounty. I don't know about you, but it makes sense to me that in a place called the hunter's paradise, the God of small predators would have greater influence than the God of gathering produce. That said, I don't doubt that humanity's adoption of agriculture has made Harvest stronger just as it has made Wolf grow weaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T00:29:03-07:00","id":860159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860073#post860073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &quot;universal&quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board? Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along?</div> </div> </div> </div>Though Pangaea fades, the hunt still has supremacy. Harvesting is in ascendance, but hasn't taken pride of place over the predators. If Pangaea survived longer than it did, who knows what it would have looked like. Father Wolf as the diminished Pangaean of the waning hunt, with Harvest dominating all as the only thing keeping billions of humans a few days from starvation and utter chaos.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:59:14-07:00","id":860256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859902#post859902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Pangaean Hearts are effectively Supernal Soul Stones that create super-demesnes and Pangaeans have easy access to the Astral Relams, the Supernal origin &quot;theory&quot; has ample evidence to establish it as setting fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not setting fact; that's *why* there are various theories.<br /> <br /> One way to consider the Pangaean use of Arcana and their hearts - humans, right. Humans can gain sustenance from consuming blood, or even be saved from death by having human blood pumped into them. They also are full of blood that vampires want to get at. That doesn't mean someone is attempting to establish 'vampire supremacy' on the mortals-only setting.<br /> <br /> Pangaeans are so powerful that they have access to some of the codes to Supernal access as<i> a minor power </i>and their sheer overwhelming immanence makes their hearts, the centre of their very being, into wellsprings of energy that are particularly of use to one type of supernatural. The true nature of Pangaeans depends on the particular Chronicle a given table is playing, and which theories (if any) the ST decides to go with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859910#post859910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If she still around Beasts would be all over her</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bUntil she harvested them for parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860073#post860073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that a Pangaean of a &quot;universal&quot; abstract concept like Harvest is weaker than animal Pangaeans. Is that true across the board?</div> </div> </div> </div> No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it because humans are only just starting to recognize agriculture and a Harvest, but have dealt with animals all along? </div> </div> </div> The role that human activity plays in the nature of Pangaeans is theoretical; certainly there are those who believe that Urfarah is suffering as humanity turns from the hunt. What is *actually* going, whether this is indeed the truth, on is up to the ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T06:24:53-07:00","id":860266,"title":"","content":"I didn't think too much of the Arcana because at the end of the day having 10 well-defined general slots for everything is way easier to get a handle of than Influence which, by their very nature, are specialized. If anything, I'd really like for Influence to be retooled and given more attention to what you can and can't do with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T07:30:47-07:00","id":860291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860256#post860256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The role that human activity plays in the nature of Pangaeans is theoretical; certainly there are those who believe that Urfarah is suffering as humanity turns from the hunt. What is *actually* going, whether this is indeed the truth, on is up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I thought that originally, that Father Wolf's weakness was due to the turn towards agriculture, I'm thinking it may be the other way around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:57:23-07:00","id":860387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=859957#post859957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already stated mine. Pangaea doesn't just bridge the gap between flesh and shadow. It is, as its name suggests, all worlds. That includes the Supernal world. Pangaeans are creatures native to a place that is at once material, terminal, vital, spiritual, temporal, auspicious, spatial, mental, dynamic, and primal. They touch the symbolic truths behind reality as easily as they touch flesh, spirit, dreams, and (in my inrerpretation) narrative, afterlife, and perhaps even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>So,assuming that your take of Pangeae as being all words is true. ,maybe that can explain why Pangaeans have many different powers. right now i'm theorizing that they have arcana,because they may be part supenal being. or maybe they something inside them that is <i>human </i>and can awaken to the supernal and use arcana like mages do. and the reason father wolf power is waning and other pangaeans are maybe becoming stronger is because they're part <i>astral! </i>and that makes them ultimately dependable in human belief and actions,that could work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-06-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:34:15-07:00","id":860418,"title":"","content":"My own thoughts on why Father Wolf is growing weak is because he's never really recovered from being poisoned and diseased. Even if humans did affect how powerful he was, I don't think that things had changed enough for him to get that noticeably bad. As for what Pangaeans are, while they might be fallen Supernal beings, I like to think that much like Mages, they just have a connection to the Supernal. I just find it suspicious how they all have different Arcana despite all being Spirit/Life or Spirit/Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T12:50:17-07:00","id":860490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860418#post860418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own thoughts on why Father Wolf is growing weak is because he's never really recovered from being poisoned and diseased. Even if humans did affect how powerful he was, I don't think that things had changed enough for him to get that noticeably bad. As for what Pangaeans are, while they might be fallen Supernal beings, I like to think that much like Mages, they just have a connection to the Supernal. I just find it suspicious how they all have different Arcana despite all being Spirit/Life or Spirit/Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, if he hadn't been poisoned and diseased, humanity wouldn't have even discovered agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T12:55:51-07:00","id":860499,"title":"","content":"If the death and weakness of the pillars made an impact on the world, the death of the Plague King, who may be Rat, may have also helped agriculture work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:00:16-07:00","id":860504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860499#post860499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the death and weakness of the pillars made an impact on the world, the death of the Plague King, who may be Rat, may have also helped agriculture work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it did a return during the Black Plague. Or an attempt at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:10:31-07:00","id":860518,"title":"","content":"Considering the numbers involved in rodents, and the devastation they wreak on food supplies, it's possible the beshilu are close to bringing the Plague King back. They may have gotten close during the time of the Black Plague, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:30:31-07:00","id":860554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=860518#post860518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the numbers involved in rodents, and the devastation they wreak on food supplies, it's possible the beshilu are close to bringing the Plague King back. They may have gotten close during the time of the Black Plague, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another interesting though: Beshilu have a mad drive to destroy the Gauntlet, which is essencially destroying Pangaea. Azlu have a mad drive to strengthen the barrier, which is essencially blocking anyone from entering or leaving Pangaea. Both are trying, on their own ways, to utterly end any chance from Mother Wolf to revive and end her hunt against them. Actually, now their mad drives to hate the Gauntlet make perfect sense, since inside the Gauntlet is Pangaea, and Pangaea is Mother Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T21:56:18-07:00","id":860783,"title":"","content":"Which rank were the firstborn,6 maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link