<strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1176401#post1176401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No on the enlightenment/intelligence/wisdom front, though. It's too abstract; the only reason one would exist would be if there was some sort of force at work that naturally uplifted species via infusing them with intelligence or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that an implied effect of the Wellspring in the Anima Mundi? The one guarded by The Last Neanderthal?<br /> <br /> Or was that only on the dreaming level, with no effect on the 'exterior' worlds? But then again, if anyone could influence / be influenced by such transcendental forces, it would be the Pangeaens...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T07:23:03-07:00","id":1202215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1199546#post1199546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> Can you help with this answers? Specially about how does an Omphalos stone works compared to a Soul Stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also interested. And... if a pangaean broke off a little bit of their heart and gave it out, what would that effect be? Is that where the bull and bird Omphalos stones came from? Then, later, the Wise got greedy and hunted down the <i>whole</i> heart for more powerful stones?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:23:35-07:00","id":1202227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1202215#post1202215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also interested. And... if a pangaean broke off a little bit of their heart and gave it out, what would that effect be? Is that where the bull and bird Omphalos stones came from? Then, later, the Wise got greedy and hunted down the <i>whole</i> heart for more powerful stones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is detailed in the Sundered World Dark Era. The availability of omphalos stones seems to be a defining factor in the sharing of information among the Wise. Since they act like soul stones, they allow access to the astral. Except they are more potent, not being subject to Dissonance and giving a nice Demesne expansion and bonus to spells of the right Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-02-2018, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T23:20:57-07:00","id":1204453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1202227#post1202227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this is detailed in the Sundered World Dark Era. The availability of omphalos stones seems to be a defining factor in the sharing of information among the Wise. Since they act like soul stones, they allow access to the astral. Except they are more potent, not being subject to Dissonance and giving a nice Demesne expansion and bonus to spells of the right Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the idea of soul stones came to the Wise by attempting to replicate Omphalos stones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T11:02:07-07:00","id":1204627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1204453#post1204453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the idea of soul stones came to the Wise by attempting to replicate Omphalos stones?</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, it isn't mentioned in the Dark Eras section, which implies that they already know about them due to them appreciating omphalos stones as more powerful and useful.<br /> <br /> The omphalos stones offered a better advantage, since Wise were somewhat anchored to humanity at the time. They weren't subject to Dissonance and the other bonuses meant that they were effectively better, if rarer and more difficult to get, than a mage's soul stone. But they had werewolves to help with the difficulty part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2018, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:21:24-07:00","id":1209686,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1199546#post1199546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a> Can you help with this answers? Specially about how does an Omphalos stone works compared to a Soul Stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, each in turn:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Do any of the Bull and Bird Omphalos stones persist to this day and age?</li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThe Seer of the Throne in the Sundered World intro certainly hopes so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's possible.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can the omphalos stone be used to coax favours from Bird and Bull?</li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Pangaeans don't adhere to the formulaic method the Orders develop for handling favours-for-soulstone-return - among other things, the Orders won't even exist for quite a while yet, and the Border Marches gods have no particular inclination to stick to some human rules.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Since Fox has a single Arcana (Mind), the Omphalos stone made from its heart will only enhance Mind spells?\u200b</li> </ol><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think this is something we never defined for certain, and I'm not 100% sure what the answer is at this stage.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:44:59-07:00","id":1209690,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>REFLECTION</b></span><br /> Reflection is a strange Pangaean, a shining divinity that is simultaneously an empty, echoing thing. It flits between the glistening raindrops, cavorts across the surfaces of still forest pools, and grimaces from the brightness of flame reflecting from human-polished metal. It hunts for profound truths so that it can reflect those truths for a little while, mimicking all manner of things from animals to rocks to concepts to other Pangaeans before eventually the hollowness at its core drives it further on in search of satisfaction. Sometimes, where it can, it reaches across to the other worlds to drive the creatures of Flesh or Spirit into mad carnivalesque endeavours of creating mirrored surfaces \u2013 digging pits to fill them with water, polishing surfaces to a sheen, bending and twisting ephemera into mirrors that catch spirits of light and flay them apart into captive images. These diversions never keep its attention any longer than pretending to be someone else does.<br /> <br /> The Wise fear Reflection, because it has shown a proclivity for infiltrating their own ranks on a whim in order to reflect whatever truths they might have managed to hoard. A circle of Wise gather in a village to discuss their discoveries and share their dreams, only to discover afterwards that it has eaten their souls and now slithers through the Border Marches in mimicry of their faces. The Uratha watch guardedly for Reflection, knowing it often comes with the rain or on those days where the light streams down through the clouds in a way that seems to render the world in stark clarity. The Uratha do not fear the Pangaean so much, for it is a source of power to them as much as a threat \u2013 a powerful prey indeed, but one that resonates closely with their nature.<br /> <br /> Reflection\u2019s true appearance tends towards semi-translucence, its flesh shivering with ripples and brief impressions of abstract shapes. Long, draping curtains of presence dangle from its turgid form, trailing around it and tapering down to their bright, splinter-sharp tips. Pulses of mirror-bright reflectiveness wash across its twisted limbs and the wide, pupil-less eyes that sit upon the palms of its many hands. Raindrops bubble up from its flesh and wash down onto the ground around it. This bizarre form is rarely seen, however, for Reflection often prefers to cloak itself in the form of something else \u2013 an illusion that the sheer, reality-warping nature of its presence renders a truth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Reflection, Bright and Empty</b></span><br /> <br /> Rank 5 Pangaean<br /> <br /> Power 15 Finesse 14 Resistance 12<br /> <br /> Willpower 10 Essence 50<br /> <br /> Initiative 26 Defence 14 Speed 26 Size 13 Corpus 25<br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Reflections 5, Water 3<br /> <br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Awe, Dement, Drain, Entropic Decay, Hallucination, Regenerate, Speed<br /> <br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Forces 1, Prime 4<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>Reflection must offer audience and refrain from hostility to anyone who comes to it wearing a mask, although it is not bound further if the offer of audience is refused or if the visitor acts against it.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> A weapon wetted in water taken from seven hundred and seventy seven natural pools that have since dried up entirely.<br /> <br /> <i>Bright Hunt: </i>If declared the target of a hunt by a pack of Uratha, Reflection may choose to gain 50 Essence in return for complying with the hunt in the form of fleeing prey. Choosing to comply constrains Reflection to forms such as prey, natural objects or phenomena; it cannot take the form of a predator or attempt to turn the hunt around against the Uratha. It may also only use the swiftness and means of escape of the forms it copies or its own Speed, and cannot use Infinite Light to evade the hunters. Should the hunters fail to catch the Pangaean within seven hundred and seventy seven minutes, the hunt immediately fails and ends; should the hunters catch the Pangaean, the first Uratha to seize Reflection in their jaws becomes able to use the Reflection of Truth ability themselves for the next seven hunred and seventy seven days. Only a single Uratha can bear this ability at any one time; Reflection cannot choose to comply with the Bright Hunt again until that time has passed. <br /> <br /> <i>Divine Bleed:</i>The first time in a scene that it suffers Corpus damage, Reflection may reflexively use the Awe, Dement, Entropic Decay or Hallucination Numina for free. It may also create a Rank 1 spirit of light or darkness for free each time it suffers damage. <br /> <br /> <i>Emptiness Within:</i> Whenever a character succeeds at a roll based on Wits, Expression or Subterfuge while in the presence of Reflection, the Pangaean gains 1 point of Essence. If Reflection spends 1 point of Willpower, it may also initiate a Reflexive Clash of Wills against the target, with success allowing it to steal their reflection; they will quite literally, no longer present a reflection in reflective surfaces. Furthermore, their normal failures at Wits, Expression and Subterfuge rolls are aggravated into dramatic failures. While it possesses a victim\u2019s reflection, the Pangaean can use Reflection of Truth to copy their appearance even while not in their presence; after seven hundred and seventy days, the reflection fades away and rips the victim\u2019s soul free from their body in the process. <br /> <br /> <i>Infinite Light:</i> Reflection can perceive through every reflective surface within seven hundred and seventy seven miles, including raindrops, the surfaces of bodies of water, copper, and obsidian. For 5 Essence, Reflection can emerge out of any such reflective surface within that range as an Instant action. <br /> <br /> <i>Monstrous Form: </i>Reflection has Armour 12, and may spend 1 Essence to shrug off any Tilt it experiences. These benefits do not apply to attacks from its Banes. <br /> <br /> <i>Overwhelming Presence:</i> A mortal human who encounters Reflection suffers an Integrity breaking point. If this roll is failed, the character gains the Madness persistent condition. <br /> <br /> <i>Reflection Of Truth: </i>As an Instant action, Reflection can copy the appearance of anything in its presence at the cost of 1 point of Essence. The copy extends to voice and other elements of the mimicked target; if Reflection copied a bird, it could sing the bird\u2019s song, fly through the air, and even alight on a branch without snapping it under the Pangaean\u2019s actually huge bulk. Reflection does not actually change shape, merely appearing to be the thing it copies; however, although this is an illusion, it is also rendered true by Reflection\u2019s power. As a result, supernatural powers that would detect illusions or lies will return the answer that it is, in fact, the thing it is pretending to be. This is not a mind-affecting power; someone who witnesses Reflection copy a target knows what they have seen. <br /> <br /> <i>Symbolic Mirror: </i>Whenever Reflection gains a Condition (or has one inflicted on it) or is the target of a supernatural effect, it can spend 5 Essence to copy the Condition or effect onto any number of additional targets as it chooses that are within seven hundred and seventy yards of its current location. After doing so, Reflection ceases to exist at its current point in time and space; instead, within seven hundred and seventy days, it will turn out to be one of the targets that the effect was copied onto, and indeed retroactively was that target all along, emerging from the chrysalis of the copied form in a shining moment of divine revelation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:50:50-07:00","id":1209692,"title":"","content":"Does Reflection also has a strange interest in radioactive energy, and has a tendency to watch things until they break in modern days? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:20:23-07:00","id":1209828,"title":"","content":"Reflection is terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:14:56-07:00","id":1209843,"title":"","content":"Terrifying.<br /> <br /> Wait, does Symbolic Mirror essentially work like demons claiming a Soul Pact and then Going Loud, in that the person copied is destroyed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:32:58-07:00","id":1209967,"title":"","content":"Yup, the target is destroyed - or rather, turns out to have ceased to exist some time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:54:43-07:00","id":1209973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1209967#post1209967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, the target is destroyed - or rather, turns out to have ceased to exist some time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice and creepy. Very demonic in the vein of the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:32:09-07:00","id":1212295,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>: I had an idea for a Pangaean so I read through Fox, Harvest and Reflection for inspiration since they are both awesome and the closest to official Pangaeans we have.<br /> I have a few questions: How do you classify the secondary powers like Divine Bleed and Monstrous Form? Dread Powers or Numina, perhaps? More importantly, how do you determine how many a given Pangaean should have? They seem to follow the guideline for the number of Numina, except Reflection falls one short.<br /> I also wonder if Divine Bleed, Monstrous Form and Overwhelming Presence apply to all Pangaeans or if it's more of a coincident all three share those.<br /> And if you don't want to answer it here, would it be a fitting request on Patreon to ask for expanded rules and guidelines to create Pangaeans? Unfortunately my income is limited, but I don't think I'm the only one who'd like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-28-2018, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T03:19:43-07:00","id":1212984,"title":"","content":"I know I intend to one day ask for a pangean in modern day. A pangean of birth and life, sort of a gaia pangean stuck in modern day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:19:53-07:00","id":1213015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1212984#post1212984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I intend to one day ask for a pangean in modern day. A pangean of birth and life, sort of a gaia pangean stuck in modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm voting Easter Bunny, if so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:55:57-07:00","id":1218635,"title":"","content":"Just so everyone knows,y'all can ask for Chris to write Pangaeans for you for five bucks on his patreon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T02:50:16-07:00","id":1223559,"title":"","content":"Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>BIRD</b></span><br /> Do not make the mistake of believing Bird is benevolent. Yes, she is the pre-eminent of the Vinca pantheon, standing alongside Bull in the eyes of the people. Yes, she has gifted splinters of her heart to the Wise, and watches over the villages and the old and the women. These things are part of who and what she is, but none of them make her kind. Bird is ancient, cold-hearted, and ice-eyed. Her vision pierces the distance, the future and the past alike. She sees the unvarnished truths of all things. She has given her patronage to humanity because she sees what is to come. She is not ancient, merely coterminous with distant aeons\u2014and those ages yet to pass. Bird plans for the future. <br /> <br /> Bird is a colossus of feathers and wings, bright staring eyes and savage talons. She is a maelstrom of avian form, carved out of flesh and strange, impressionistic shapes. The very presence of Bird warps the world around her, extending or contracting distances\u2014especially dizzying heights and plunging drops. The Pangaean takes a cruel pleasure in inflicting pain upon those who cross her path and displease her; her claws can flay a human with trivial ease, plucking out pulsating organs to observe and consider with clinically cold interest. Sometimes, Bird comes in other forms\u2014a woman, a flock of brightly-plumaged birds, a storm\u2014but she is in no way diminished in these shapes. She remains a god, capable of crushing one of the Wise with a finger even if appearing as a slender girl. <br /> <br /> Bird, like Bull, often slips into Flesh and Shadow to perpetrate her schemes. She does so only on swift jaunts, cloaking herself from the piercing gaze of Wolf as best she can. The Pangaean respects and fears the boundary god despite her power; where stubborn, belligerent Bull will openly clash with the Great Predator until he is exhausted and can be dragged back into Pangaea in Wolf\u2019s jaws, Bird has no such intention of letting herself be weakened in open conflict. Better to orchestrate her plans quietly, so that she can lay foundations that will bear fruit in millennia to come without interference. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bird, Cerulean and Cruel</span></b><br /> Rank 7 Pangaean<br /> <br /> As a Rank 7 entity, Bird does not operate within the usual rules framework. Her capabilities cannot be reduced to a few dice pools. Still, she possesses several characteristics that are worth noting, and her mere presence can radically influence a scene. <br /> <br /> <b>Influences:</b> Birds 7, Change 4, Cruelty 3 <br /> <b>Arcana: </b>Time 5, Space 2 <br /> <b>Ban: </b>Bird must offer audience and refrain from hostility to anyone who comes to her wearing blue, although she is not bound further if the offer of audience is refused or if the visitor acts against it. <br /> <b>Bane:</b> Bird\u2019s Bane is no longer part of reality; she still has a Bane, but supernatural attempts to determine specifically what it is are met only with the sense of a frayed edge where the Pangaean tore the concept out of existence. <br /> <br /> <i>Cruel Grasp:</i> Whenever a character succeeds at a roll involving acting cruelly to another or causing them harm in the presence of Bird, the Pangaean gains 1 point of Essence. She may, if she wishes, initiate a Clash of Wills against the target which, being a divinity, she wins. This causes the target to no longer be anchored in time, moving their existence to any other point in time that Bird is coterminous with that she chooses. She may also, if she wishes, tear their soul out in the process; souls acquired in this way might be tortured, eaten, shoved into birds, used to create bizarre avian Claimed, or also moved to another point in time and placed in the body of an unsuspecting victim who finds themselves overwritten by the soul and personality of someone from an entirely different era. She may spend a Willpower point to extend the range on this power to the entire globe, rather than just her immediate presence. <br /> <br /> <i>Fateful Patterns:</i> Any supernatural powers that provide auguries, seek to predict destinies, or offer up answers as to fate\u2019s plans benefit from the rote quality if used in Bird\u2019s presence. Doing so causes Bird to suffer an injury that spills blood and screaming avians, scabbing over in a canker of wildly staring eyes. Bird also becomes aware of the information gleaned by the power and can, if she chooses, retroactively cause the power to dramatically fail instead; she still retains the knowledge gained but the diviner will not, and will suffer the usual consequences of a dramatic failure. <br /> <br /> <i>Feather Transmogrification: </i>A character who is injured in the presence of Bird bleeds bloody feathers, a grisly experience that leaves the victim with quills stabbing into their wounds. The corpse of a character who perishes erupts into a flock of ravenous birds, each flying away with a scrap of carrion in their claws and beaks. Rarely, instead, it creates an avian monstrosity with something of the guise of a human. A character who leaves Bird wounded and with feathers still budding from their raw meat will lose a memory or have some facet of their personality permanently change; if they are clear-minded and focused, a successful Resolve + Composure roll allows them to choose what they lose or change before it takes effect. <br /> <br /> <i>Many Shapes: </i>As well as her normal form, Bird has many other shapes, all of which possess the same attributes and abilities and which it costs nothing for her to shift to. As well as her large, true shape, Bird can take the form of a normal bird, a normal human, an otherworldly blend of human and divine avian, a flock of birds, a storm, a bolt of lightning, a sense of cruel satisfaction in the suffering of others, the gleaming light on a knife\u2019s sharp edge, or the sudden realization that one has been manipulated into serving the agenda of another. In her more abstract forms, Bird has no immediate physical substance, but is still just as capable of acting. <br /> <br /> <i>Overwhelming Presence:</i> A mortal human who encounters Bird suffers an Integrity breaking point. If this roll is failed, the character gains the Madness persistent condition. <br /> <br /> <i>Perspective Dominion: </i>By observing a thing, Bird can cause its effective Size to be divided by up to 7 or multiplied up to 7, and can alter her perspective on the target reflexively to change the extent of this effect at any time. <br /> <br /> <i>Sunder Kindness:</i> A character in Bird\u2019s presence cannot regain Willpower or Mana from any act that involves kindness, charity, or mercy towards another. Supernatural powers that would bestow healing on another instead inflict the damage they would restore onto the character. Speaking a kind word for another causes one of the character\u2019s eyes to squirm then pop out of their skull; a bird pushes itself free from the meat of the socket, slick with blood and with the eye firmly in its beak, dealing 1 point of aggravated damage and obviously blinding the character in that eye. If the bird is able to fly away and swallow the eyeball, it will forever see what the character sees with their remaining eye, and will chatter and sing any secrets they see to Bird.<br /> <br /> <i>Vertigo Warp: </i>When Bird is present in a scene, all distances up and down are quadrupled, except for movement by flight. This can make small drops into lethal falls. If Bird wishes, she can alter which direction is down at will. Bird possesses many other capabilities, but they largely pertain to the dealings and interactions of godly beings and are of little concern to those of the world of Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T02:58:35-07:00","id":1223560,"title":"","content":"Yay!<br /> <br /> Will read a moment later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <br /> <br /> Sunder Kindness may be the source of the Halaku, Fateful Patterns and Perspective Dominion sounds like how the Perspective came to be, and Cruel Grasp is just plain <i>delicious</i> to use in a story. And the general emphasis on cruel avians make me wonder if a part of Bird is in or is a certain Dark Place...<br /> <br /> Oh, and it seems Overwhelming Presence is the only truly universal Pangaean power. Perhaps Divine Bleed and Monstrous Form are for supplementing lesser Pangaean\u2019s immediate \u201cencounter level?\u201d And Many Shapes fittingly sounds like something animal-like Pangaeans share. Oh, and it seems every Pangaean so far also has a \u201cscrew with souls\u201d power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-31-2018, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:06:12-07:00","id":1223660,"title":"","content":"I find birds very creepy, this certainly doesn't help. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:18:22-07:00","id":1223664,"title":"","content":"Bird <u><b>is</b></u> the word. How the hell did the Wise convince that thing to help them? <br /> <br /> Also, I like how Cruel Grasp is such an excellent excuse to have temporally displaced characters, both forwards and backwards in time. The non-tangible forms BIrd can take are also cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:27:03-07:00","id":1223665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1223664#post1223664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bird <u><b>is</b></u> the word. How the hell did the Wise convince that thing to help them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like it <i>gifted </i>the Wise with heart-stones to begin with, the Wise not being involved with it and, when asking for more, were rejected.<br /> <br /> Given the cruel and plotting nature of Bird it doesn't take too much of a leap to figure out the why. Mages see omphalos stones, mages start wanting more, mages reap Fox and others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T10:29:09-07:00","id":1223667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=1223665#post1223665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div>